window.TC_PORTRAITS=Object.assign(window.TC_PORTRAITS||{},{"gemini-aries-aries":["You are already halfway through the door, asking a question over your shoulder, and the answer will have to catch up. The Aries Rising leads with the body: quick, direct, forward-leaning, ready before anyone has finished introducing you. The Aries Moon needs the same thing from the inside, momentum and honesty and room to react, so the feeling and the face match. Your Gemini Sun supplies the talk, the jokes and a dozen reasons to try the next thing. People meet readiness. Only later do they notice how fast you are learning.","Two of your lights sit in Aries, so the feeling and the manner move together, with no gap between what you need and how you arrive, and no outside view of how fast that looks. The Gemini Sun makes a friendly sextile to both, so curiosity helps the fire along rather than arguing with it. Mars rules the pair. What this chart lacks is a pause: it can have an opinion, a plan and a first step before a second thought has been invited.","Quick courage with a mind behind it. You start conversations, projects and arguments with equal ease, you learn on the move, and you are rarely embarrassed by being a beginner. People find you refreshing, and often follow you to places they would never have planned.","Speed becomes the habit and the habit becomes a style, so every feeling is acted on and every question answered before it is understood. Impatience can read as dismissal. Growth is a deliberate beat before replying, in which you ask what the other person actually said."],"gemini-aries-taurus":["People hear the low, unhurried voice and assume the mind behind it is just as unhurried. They have not seen the Gemini Sun running three trains of thought at once, or the Aries Moon with a hand already on the emergency cord. The Taurus Rising is real: it slows the room, softens the delivery and makes you look as if you have all afternoon. Inside, you are impatient to ask, try and move. The voice and the impatience tend to arrive together, and people forgive the second because of the first.","Aries, Taurus and Gemini are three neighbouring signs, so each light sees only the one beside it: the Aries Moon barely meets the Gemini Sun, and the Taurus Rising stands between them like a well-mannered doorman. Sun and Moon are a friendly sextile, so thought and feeling cooperate quickly. The Rising slows the delivery rather than the speed. Venus rules the manner and Mars the need, which gives you gentleness at the door and a flare in the kitchen.","A calm front with a fast engine. You can say a bold thing in a way that is easy to hear, start something with energy and let the manner keep the peace. You are persuasive, warm and good at making an urgent idea feel safe to adopt.","The pleasant voice can hide impatience until it has become irritation, and the Moon’s anger arrives as a tight smile. Growth is letting the speed show a little, early, so that people learn the real tempo, and saying the plain sentence in the same lovely voice."],"gemini-aries-gemini":["The first minute at a party is where you shine: the question is already asked, the joke is told and you have found the one guest who will argue back. The Gemini Rising arrives talking, with quick hands and an eye on the next doorway. Your Gemini Sun is the same mind in daylight, curious about everything at once. The Aries Moon sets off before the sentence is finished, so what looks like charm is also appetite. You are frank, fast and hard to bore, and often a little out of breath.","Sun and Rising share Gemini, so mind and manner speak with one voice, and the Aries Moon sits a sextile away from both. That is an easy, quick friendship between three lights, not a quarrel. Mercury rules the face and Mars the need, which makes thought fast and feeling faster. Because the arrangement runs so smoothly, nothing in it asks you to slow down. The Moon supplies the push, the Sun finds the words and the Rising delivers them before the Moon has finished deciding what it wanted.","Instant traction. You can start a conversation, a project or a rumour of a good idea in the time it takes others to find their coat, and you say plainly what you want. You are funny under pressure, generous with attention and good at turning a stalled gathering into a moving one.","Speed becomes habit, and you can leave a sentence, a plan or a friend before the middle of it has been understood. Anger arrives clean and clears quickly, but the words it used stay in other people’s memory. Growth is finishing one thing at the pace it asks for, and letting the pause after a remark be part of the remark."],"gemini-aries-cancer":["When you are cornered you get funny first and furious second, and the fury is usually over before the joke has landed. People meet a softer face than that. The Cancer Rising asks whether you have eaten, remembers the dog’s name and keeps the first remark gentle. The Gemini Sun offers a quick mind steering the talk, trading a fact for a story. Then the Aries Moon speaks, bluntly and warmly, and the room learns that the kindness has a pulse and a temper.","Cancer Rising is ruled by the Moon, so your Aries Moon governs the whole chart: the need steers, and the gentle front is only the way in. Moon and Rising are both cardinal and their elements clash, fire against water, which makes steam when you are tired. The Gemini Sun sits in an easy sextile to the Moon and finds words fast, so a burst of temper gets a clever sentence before the Rising can soften it. You then spend the evening editing that sentence.","Honest tenderness. You can say the true thing while holding someone’s hand, and you recover from a quarrel faster than almost anyone. You are quick to the door when someone is hurt, funny enough to lower the stakes, and unwilling to sulk afterwards.","The soft front and the temper take turns, and neither gets to finish. You apologise before you have stopped being angry, so the point is dropped to keep the peace. Or you snap at someone and then fuss over them to make amends. Growth is letting the anger say its whole sentence calmly and out loud, and trusting the friendship to survive it."],"gemini-aries-leo":["Three tenants share one house and none of them wants to wait. The Gemini Sun sits at the front desk with the news, already half into the next sentence. The Aries Moon stands by the door with its boots on, wanting momentum and honesty and hating a cornered corridor. The Leo Rising steps onto the balcony and waves, and the whole street looks up. People feel the heat of it before they have heard a word.","This is an arc of ease: two sextiles bridged by a trine, fire and air feeding each other round the wheel. Moon and Rising are both fire and agree that life should be lived out loud, while the Sun supplies the script. The Sun also rules your Leo Rising, which makes your quick mind the chart ruler, so the entrance is a spoken one. Nothing in the geometry argues, and so nothing in it says wait.","Contagious enthusiasm. You can walk into a flat evening and give it a plot, say the daring thing with a smile and make people feel brave by proximity. You are generous with credit, quick to apologise and good at turning a wish into a Saturday.","With every light pointing the same way, nobody supplies a brake. You commit aloud before checking the diary, and move on from a mood or a person before the other party has caught up. Anger clears fast, but the speech it used lingers. Growth is a pause the length of one breath, and asking what someone else thinks before announcing what you do."],"gemini-aries-virgo":["At the door, hand already on the latch, you stop to straighten the shoes on the mat, then leave at a run. People meet the Virgo Rising first: neat, observant, modest, the one who noticed the draught and has a view about the filter. Your Gemini Sun supplies a quick mind that asks the next question. The Aries Moon is the reason for the running. It needs momentum and plain speech, and a fence, a queue or a corrected sentence can make it bristle in a second and forgive in two.","Mercury rules both your Sun and your Rising, so mind and manner share a planet, yet they stand in square: one wants to range, the other wants to sort, and both are mutable enough to keep arguing about it. The Aries Moon is in sextile with the Sun, so need and curiosity cooperate and go fast. It shares neither element nor mode with the Rising, a quincunx, so the neat front and the quick feeling keep making small, slightly irritated adjustments to each other.","Fast, useful honesty. You can spot the error, say it kindly and fix it before the meeting starts, and you recover from a disagreement faster than anyone expects. You are good in an emergency, good with a list and very good at being straightforward without being rude.","Criticism and impatience can arrive in the same breath. You may correct a small thing sharply when the real upset was elsewhere, then tidy the room to make amends. A neat surface can hide how quickly you want to leave. Growth is saying “I am annoyed” before the remark about the dishes, and finishing one thing before the next begins."],"gemini-aries-libra":["People assume you are the soft, agreeable one, because you arrive with such good manners and so much attention for everyone’s chair. What they have not seen is what happens when something unfair is allowed to stand. The Libra Rising is gracious, symmetrical and charming. Your Gemini Sun is quick, curious and fond of a good argument held politely. The Aries Moon is the point of the spear: it needs momentum and honesty, flares fast, clears fast and takes being cornered as the one real injury.","Moon and Rising face each other across the wheel in opposition, Aries against Libra, self against other: the need wants to act now and the manner wants to consult first. Both are cardinal, so neither is passive, and the room hears a polite sentence with a sharp edge on it. The Sun in Gemini is a trine from the Rising and a sextile from the Moon, so it speaks both languages and makes a good arbitrator, which is the job you are always being handed.","Courteous courage. You can say the true thing in a way that is difficult to resent, and you will stand up for a stranger who is being treated badly without making a scene about it. You decide fast, listen well and clear the air before it thickens.","The pendulum between the two chairs is wide. You may agree to a plan you dislike and then flare at something small, or hold a charming silence that is really a refusal. Anger comes out clean but is sometimes aimed at the nearest person. Growth is saying the plain no at the first moment you feel it, with the manners still on."],"gemini-aries-scorpio":["The hour that matters is the one right after someone is unfair to you: you say nothing, a letter writes itself in your head, and by morning it has been sent, burned or forgotten. The Scorpio Rising holds the face still and the gaze steady, so people feel read and cannot say why. The Gemini Sun adds a quick, curious mind that keeps asking. The Aries Moon is the flint: feelings arrive fast and clean, and being cornered is the one real injury.","This is a yod by sign: Sun and Moon stand in an easy sextile, and both stand a quincunx from the Rising, so the two lights that talk and strike share nothing with the guarded face. Mars rules both the Aries Moon and the Scorpio Rising, so the temper and the stillness are one planet in two moods: the strike and the held breath. The Sun, whose job is to explain, keeps adjusting the explanation to a manner it cannot quite reach.","Decisive depth. You can see a lie quickly, say so plainly and stay loyal to the people who pass the test. You act in a crisis with a clear head, you say less than you know and you can start again once the air has cleared.","The gap between the flare and the file is where the trouble sits. You may swallow the anger and let it harden into a very polite distance, or flash at someone who did nothing. Words meant to clear the air stay in other people’s memory. Growth is speaking while the feeling is clean, and not waiting for the letter to be written."],"gemini-aries-sagittarius":["You say yes before the question is finished, and you find out what you agreed to on the way there. The Sagittarius Rising is open, bright and restless: you arrive laughing, with news or a story, and people feel invited to widen their lives. Your Gemini Sun is the curious mind collecting more of it. The Aries Moon is the drum under the whole procession, needing momentum, honesty and room to react, and clearing its anger as fast as it flares.","Two of your three lights are fire and in trine, the Aries Moon and the Sagittarius Rising, so the need and the manner run in the same direction at the same speed. The Gemini Sun stands in sextile to the Moon and in opposition to the Rising: the mind that asks faces the manner that already has the answer, and the Moon backs whichever moves first. Jupiter rules the manner, which is why the invitation is so large.","Infectious go. You can start a trip, a conversation or a movement with one sentence, make a risk sound like a good afternoon and stay cheerful when the plan changes. You say what you mean, forgive fast and bring other people along.","Three lights that agree on speed leave no one at the brakes. You may commit before the details arrive, and move on from the mess before it is cleared up. Anger clears quickly, but the words it used take longer. Growth is reading the second paragraph before you say yes, and finishing one thing that is boring."],"gemini-aries-capricorn":["The building has three tenants and they want different things. The Gemini Sun is the clerk at the front window, trading a whispered rumour for a better one. The Capricorn Rising is the senior partner in the corner office, composed, dry, a little older than the calendar and hard to reach. The Aries Moon is in the stairwell in running shoes, needing momentum and room to react. Visitors meet the office and, eventually, hear the footsteps.","The Aries Moon and the Capricorn Rising are both cardinal and in square, fire against earth, so the impulse and the poise pull against each other every working day. The Moon wants to go now and the Rising wants it done properly, which is a held sprint. The Gemini Sun is a sextile from the Moon, so wit and speed cooperate, and a quincunx from the Rising, so the mind and the gravity never quite meet. You are quick in the head and slow to show it.","Controlled drive. You can start fast and finish properly, keep calm in a crisis and say the difficult thing in a dry sentence that makes people laugh and then listen. People trust your timing and your word.","The held sprint can leak. You may sit on an irritation until it has become a decision, then deliver it with great calm and no warning. Being cornered is the real injury, and the composed face can hide how fast the feeling arrived. Growth is letting the anger out at its own size, early, and letting someone see you move."],"gemini-aries-aquarius":["One hand on the latch of a party you are not quite attending, you decide with a grin whether to come in. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance, a little ahead of the present moment. The Gemini Sun is the curious mind that has already worked out who is inside. The Aries Moon needs momentum and honesty, flares fast, clears fast and takes being cornered as the real injury. So the gate stays unlatched.","This is an arc of ease: two sextiles bridged by a trine, air and fire in friendly conversation round the wheel. The Sun and the Rising are both air and speak the same quick language, and the fire of the Moon is on good terms with each of them. Nothing in the geometry puts up a fence. What you are, what you need and how you arrive all want freedom and a little speed, which makes an easy life to start and a hard one to slow down.","Frank freedom. You can say what you think without making an enemy, welcome a new idea and move on without a grudge. You are quick to defend a friend, quick to forgive and good at starting something with strangers. People feel free around you.","With every light favouring speed and room, nobody in the house asks for the long haul. You may leave before the promise is tested, call the leaving independence and be surprised that someone minded. Anger clears, and the distance it opened can stay. Growth is staying through one slow, ordinary stretch with a person or a project, and finding out what it gives."],"gemini-aries-pisces":["People take you for the soft one who goes where the day takes them: dreamy, agreeable, hard to pin to a plan. The truth is that you decided what you wanted before the sentence was finished. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and a little faraway, and people project onto it freely. Your Gemini Sun is the curious mind quietly collecting evidence. The Aries Moon is the first stroke of the brush: it needs momentum and honesty, and flares fast and clears fast.","The Gemini Sun is a square from the Pisces Rising, both mutable, air against water: the mind wants to name and the manner wants to blur, so the first impression is always a little out of focus. The Aries Moon stands in sextile with the Sun, so the speed and the sentence cooperate, and a semi-sextile from the Rising, which barely notices it. The gentle face is a surface and the Moon is a decision. People are surprised by the speed of the second.","Soft power. You can disarm a room with gentleness and then say exactly what you mean, change direction cleanly and be generous without being a doormat. People feel safe around you and are startled, pleasantly, by your clarity.","The blur and the brushstroke take turns. You may let people project onto you for weeks and then react sharply to the thing they projected, or avoid a conflict until it flares at the wrong target. Being cornered is the real injury. Growth is saying the plain yes or no in the first minute, while the face is still gentle."],"gemini-taurus-aries":["Nobody in the room speaks faster, and nobody can hurry you to lunch. The Aries Rising arrives at speed, direct and ready, with a Gemini Sun that has three questions and a joke prepared. Then the Taurus Moon asserts itself: it needs a proper meal, a chair that fits and a body at ease, and it will wait for these with the calm of an old tree. People assume you are all motion. You are a fast mind in a slow-feeling body, and you eat as though the afternoon depended on it.","Aries, Taurus and Gemini are three neighbouring signs, so each light sees only the one beside it: the Rising barely notices that the Moon is a sign away, and the Moon barely hears the Sun. The Sun and Rising are a friendly sextile, so quick things line up easily. The Taurus Moon, exalted and comfortable, is the light that wants nothing to change. Mars hurries the manner, Venus slows the need, and Mercury interprets between them, usually with a joke.","Speed with staying power. You can think on your feet and then sit down and finish the job. You are sociable, sensual and strikingly practical for someone so curious, and you give people the sense of being entertained and looked after in the same evening.","The face runs ahead, the Moon digs its heels in behind it, and the Sun explains both with a good story. You may agree to the new plan with your whole manner while your body quietly refuses it. Growth is checking with the Moon first, asking whether this is comfortable, and letting the answer set the pace."],"gemini-taurus-taurus":["You carry it in the shoulders and the throat: shoulders that drop when the room is comfortable, and a throat that opens when the conversation is good. Moon and Rising both sit in Taurus, so the feeling and the face are calm, sensual and unhurried, fond of good food, soft fabric and routine. Your Gemini Sun is the bird in the courtyard of this settled house, asking questions, trading news and chasing every new thing that flies over. The house stays still. The bird goes out and comes back with something to say.","Moon and Rising share Taurus, so the need and the manner are one calm voice, with no gap and no outside view: you are exactly as unhurried as you seem. The Gemini Sun is a neighbour to both, so it barely sees what its own house is doing, and the chart holds a curious mind surrounded by two lights that want things to stay. Venus rules the pair and the Moon is exalted, which gives comfort a deep authority. Mercury has to argue its case with charm.","Soothing intelligence. You can explain anything in a way that feels like a hand on the shoulder, you are good with money, food, voices and the pace of a room, and you bring ideas into the world without upsetting it. People relax near you and then discover how much they have learned.","Two comfortable lights can outvote the curious one, so questions get postponed in favour of the routine. The Sun then talks about change at length without altering the furniture. Growth is one real experiment a month, something that makes the body slightly uncomfortable, and staying with it long enough to learn from it."],"gemini-taurus-gemini":["Picture a telegraph wire strung between two apple trees: quick messages crossing a slow orchard. That is how you work. The Gemini Rising talks first, lightly and well, and the Gemini Sun keeps the lines busy with questions, news and plans. But the Taurus Moon wants fruit, routine and a body at ease, so every bright idea is tested against whether it can be lived in. You seem airy at the door and turn out to be loyal, sensual and difficult to move.","The Taurus Moon is exalted and sits one sign before both the Sun and the Rising, a semi-sextile, so it barely sees either of them: neighbours who share a fence and rarely meet. The Moon wants comfort without commentary, while the Sun and the Rising want to say everything aloud. Venus rules the need and Mercury the manner, a pair who get on charmingly in company and drift apart at home. You can feel slow inside a quick face, and the quick face hides how settled you want to be.","Practical curiosity. You can learn a subject and then make it useful: cook from a new cuisine, build the shelf, explain the contract. Your voice is warm, your timing is good and your taste is reliable. People trust you with ideas because you also bring dinner.","The comfortable Moon can quietly veto the restless Sun, and the veto sounds like a joke: maybe later. Plans pile up unsent. The reverse also happens, with the mind bored by a routine the body loves. Growth is naming which light is speaking before you choose, and letting one small experiment into the week without a long debate."],"gemini-taurus-cancer":["Can I stay in tonight and still be interesting? You ask it often, and the answer is usually yes, with something on the stove. The Cancer Rising welcomes people with attention, small kindnesses and a spare chair. The Gemini Sun is curious about everything, quick with a fact and happy to swap it for a story. Behind both, the exalted Taurus Moon wants a settled routine, good food and a body at ease. You seem light and turn out to be warm, loyal and difficult to hurry.","The Taurus Moon is exalted, an honoured guest, and it sits two signs from the Rising in a sextile, so the need and the welcome agree about nearly everything: food, shelter, a calm room. The Gemini Sun is the odd one out, a semi-sextile from both and the neighbour who sees neither clearly. All three lights differ in element and in mode, so nothing doubles and nothing backs the mind up. The home runs smoothly while the curiosity keeps stepping out to ask about the weather elsewhere.","Comfort with a bright mind in it. You can make a home that is easy to rest in and then fill it with good talk. You remember the dish a friend loves and the question they asked last month, and your calm is believable because you have lived in it.","Safety can become the answer to every question. You may decline the new person, trip or idea because the sofa is warm and the reason sounds sensible, while the mind paces. Slow to anger and slower to forgive, you can also keep a grievance as carefully as a jar of preserves. Growth is one small new thing each month, tasted before it is judged, and one old grievance opened and let go."],"gemini-taurus-leo":["In ten years you will see that you were never tired of people, only of being on all the time, and that the cure was a very ordinary Tuesday. For now the Leo Rising arrives warm and well lit, with a gift for entrances and a laugh that fills a doorway. Your Gemini Sun supplies the talk, bright and well sourced. Behind both sits an exalted Taurus Moon that wants good bread, a soft chair and a routine nobody applauds. The audience gets the show, and the body keeps asking for the interval.","Taurus Moon and Leo Rising are both fixed and in square, earth against fire, so the stage and the sofa argue about every evening and neither gives way. The Sun in Gemini, a sextile from the Rising and a semi-sextile from the Moon, carries messages between them and finds both amusing. It runs the performance, since it rules the Leo Rising, but the Moon is exalted and stubborn, and it decides when the performance ends.","Warmth you can lean on. You can host the big night and also stay for the washing up, and you make people feel looked at and looked after. Your taste is good, your word is reliable and your talk has a body in it: food, colour, texture, the right chair.","Stubbornness speaks in two voices, pride at the front and comfort behind it. You may refuse a change because it would mean being seen unprepared, or cling to a pleasure long after it stopped pleasing. A slow grudge can sit behind a bright smile. Growth is letting the interval be a real one, and changing one fixed habit this year just to see who you are without it."],"gemini-taurus-virgo":["You have the quickest mind and the most settled body you know, and each keeps the other honest. The Virgo Rising is neat, observant and modest, quick to spot what needs doing and happy to do it without announcing it. The Gemini Sun makes the conversation quick and the reading list long. The exalted Taurus Moon wants a routine, a good meal and a body at ease, and nothing about the day goes well without them. You look efficient and live like someone who loves a long breakfast.","The Taurus Moon and the Virgo Rising are both earth and in trine, so need and manner agree: order, comfort and a task done well are the same pleasure. The Gemini Sun is the odd one out, a square from the Rising, sharing its ruling planet but not its pace, and a semi-sextile from the Moon, which barely sees it. The household of body and manner is calm and competent, and the mind keeps arriving with new plans that must be fitted into the schedule.","Craft with ease. You can learn something quickly and then do it beautifully, whether it is cooking, repairing or arranging, to a high standard and without a fuss. People trust your hands as much as your opinions, and your calm is the kind that others borrow without asking.","Routine can win every argument against the new idea, and the mind then circles in its corner. You may fuss over small matters to avoid the larger, riskier choice, and a slow grudge can hide behind helpfulness. Growth is changing one habit a month on purpose, and letting a plan stay rough for a day before it is made correct."],"gemini-taurus-libra":["Your shoulders drop half an inch when the room is pleasant, and when it is not, you go very still, hands folded, like someone at a recital. The Libra Rising is gracious, symmetrical and charming: the right word, the right distance, flowers on the table. The Gemini Sun keeps the talk airy and informed. The Taurus Moon, exalted and quiet, is what the body is listening to. It needs safety you can touch, good food and a routine that lets the evening be slow.","Venus rules both your Taurus Moon and your Libra Rising, so what you need and how you arrive share a planet and a taste: you want things to be beautiful and to last. The two still do not see each other, a quincunx with no element or mode in common, so a gracious front keeps adjusting to a body that wants to stay put. The Gemini Sun is in trine with the Rising and a semi-sextile from the Moon, so the mind talks easily with the face and rarely with the stomach.","Taste that can be lived in. You can set a table, choose a colour or pour a drink so that people feel cared for and unhurried. Your charm has body to it. People find you easy and substantial, a rare pair, and your word, once given, is reliable and warm.","Comfort and courtesy can combine into avoidance. You may put off the awkward conversation until the meal is finished, and then the next meal, and slow to anger becomes slow to speak. A grievance can sit under the tablecloth for months. Growth is naming the thing over the first course rather than the last."],"gemini-taurus-scorpio":["A well worn footpath is a record of where feet went, and a scar can become a map of where it hurt and how it healed. You are made of both. The Scorpio Rising gives you a still, probing look that people feel before they understand it. The Gemini Sun is the quick mind that keeps asking. The exalted Taurus Moon wants routine, good food and a body at ease, and it is slow to anger and slower to forgive. You change your mind rarely, and you remember everything that led there.","Moon and Rising are in opposition and both fixed, Taurus against Scorpio, the axis of what we keep and what we transform. The Moon wants to hold on to comfort and the Rising wants to see through it, so the home is pleasant and the stare unsettling. The Gemini Sun is a semi-sextile from the Moon and a quincunx from the Rising, so it has no natural partner among your lights and spends its life translating between two stubborn ones.","Loyalty with open eyes. You can hold a friend through a long bad stretch, see through a charming story and make a home that is both comfortable and honest. Your word is kept, your senses are good and you are very hard to hustle.","Two fixed lights make a very long memory. You may hold a position for years because letting go would feel like losing face, and keep an old hurt warm in the pantry. The mind makes a joke to cover it. Growth is changing one settled opinion on purpose, and burying one old grudge with a small ceremony."],"gemini-taurus-sagittarius":["Can I have the road and the kitchen both? You ask it at every airport and again at every bakery. The Sagittarius Rising arrives bright and restless, laughing, with news, and people feel invited to widen their lives. The Gemini Sun supplies a quick mind that wants to know what is over the hill. The exalted Taurus Moon wants bread, routine and a body at ease, and it is slow to anger and slower to forgive. You travel well because you take the comfort with you.","Sun and Rising are in opposition, Gemini asking and Sagittarius answering, and the Taurus Moon is a semi-sextile from the Sun and a quincunx from the Rising, so it fits neither of them well. All three lights differ in element, and the two mutable ones keep inviting the fixed one to move. The Moon is exalted and stubborn: it will go, but only with a proper breakfast and a way home.","Worldly comfort. You can make a stranger’s kitchen feel like yours, cook for a crowd on a camping stove and turn a delayed train into a picnic. You learn a place quickly and love it slowly, and you bring home recipes, phrases and friends.","Comfort makes a good excuse not to go, and enthusiasm a good excuse not to stay. You may talk for a year about a journey while the sofa wins, or leave a good thing out of restlessness and miss it by noon. Slow to anger, slower to forgive, you can also keep a quarrel in the luggage. Growth is choosing the trip and the home on purpose, one at a time."],"gemini-taurus-capricorn":["At fifty you will understand that the gravity you wore at twenty was borrowed, and that the lightness you kept in your pocket was the real inheritance. For now the Capricorn Rising is composed, dry and a little older than the calendar, and people trust you before they know you. The Gemini Sun is the quick, curious mind with a joke ready. The exalted Taurus Moon wants good bread, a steady routine and a body at ease. You climb slowly, with snacks, and arrive in good condition.","The Taurus Moon and the Capricorn Rising are both earth and in trine, so need and manner agree about patience, quality and the long way round. The Gemini Sun is the odd one out: a semi-sextile from the Moon, which barely sees it, and a quincunx from the Rising, which shares neither its element nor its mode. The mind is the only light that wants to hurry, and the other two have the weight to say no. The house is calm, and the Sun keeps proposing a detour.","Solid charm. You can build something that lasts, enjoy the building and tell a good story on the way. Your word is kept, your hands are capable and your calm is real. People lean on you and find you funnier than they expected.","Two heavy lights can outvote the bright one. You may keep to the sensible path and let the questions go unasked, or hold a grievance with great composure for years. Comfort and duty make a good argument for staying put. Growth is taking one unplanned turn a month, and letting the Sun choose the route."],"gemini-taurus-aquarius":["You live in next year and you need your breakfast exactly as it was, and you do not see a contradiction. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance, a person slightly ahead of the present moment. The Gemini Sun brings a quick mind trading in news and rumour. The exalted Taurus Moon is the old oak table: it needs routine, good food and a body at ease, and it is slow to anger and slower to forgive. You are the traveller with a favourite mug.","The Taurus Moon and the Aquarius Rising are both fixed and in square, earth against air: the need wants things to stay and the manner wants them to change, so the table is polished while the future is drawn up in the next room. The Gemini Sun is in trine with the Rising and a semi-sextile from the Moon, so mind and manner converse easily and neither can see the Moon well. A door with no handle on the outside keeps the comfort private.","Stable originality. You can try a new idea and build it into a habit, make the unconventional feel like home and bring good bread to a strange meeting. Your instincts are solid, your tastes are lasting and your friendships hold.","The fixed pair is stubborn in two directions. You may defend an odd opinion and an old routine with the same heat, or keep a grievance as a principle. The mind jokes about it. Growth is changing one settled habit on purpose, and telling one friend the thing you have been polishing instead of saying."],"gemini-taurus-pisces":["The feeling settles in your belly, in the soft place under the ribs, and your hands go quiet and warm around whatever they are holding. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and faraway, a face people project onto. Your Gemini Sun brings a quick, curious mind that keeps the conversation lively. The exalted Taurus Moon needs safety you can touch: routine, good food, a body at ease. It is slow to anger and slower to forgive, and consoled by beauty and repetition, like a bell heard across a valley.","The Taurus Moon is a sextile from the Pisces Rising, earth and water working as partners, so feeling and manner are on easy terms: the softness has somewhere to land, and the comfort has somewhere to dream. The Gemini Sun is the third light, a square from the Rising and a semi-sextile from the Moon, so the quick mind is the one slightly out of step with a warm, slow household. All three differ in element, and two are mutable.","Sensory kindness. You can make a place feel gentle: the light, the food, the music, the right voice at the right hour. You offer comfort without effort and company without pressure, and your loyalty is tender and steady.","Comfort can be a refuge from decisions. You may stay in a pleasant mood for a long time, let the mind talk about change while the body declines it and keep a quiet grudge in the pantry. The face stays gentle through all of it. Growth is one small leap a month, and naming what you want before you have been fed."],"gemini-gemini-aries":["People assume you talk too much to be serious. Talking is simply how you think. Sun and Moon both sit in Gemini, so the self and the need share one curious voice that learns by saying things aloud, trying them on and trading them for better ones. The Aries Rising gives that voice a running start: you arrive mid-sentence, with a question already in your hand. The result is quick, funny and sometimes more honest than intended. The seriousness shows up in the follow-through.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, so mind and feeling use the same channel: what you feel arrives as a sentence, and what you think arrives as a mood. There is no gap and no outside view, so the chart rarely hears a dissenting voice. The Aries Rising is a friendly sextile to both and gives the pair a body: speed, a direct manner, a readiness to act on the idea in the same minute. Mercury rules the doubled light and Mars the entrance, so the words come armed.","Verbal courage. You say the thing nobody else will, you ask the naive question that cracks the problem open and you learn from every answer. You are an excellent starter of conversations, movements and friendships, and your enthusiasm is usually contagious.","A doubled Gemini can talk its way past a feeling, and the Rising helps it get away faster. You may announce a decision to avoid having a mood about it. Growth is staying silent for one full minute after something hurts, and noticing what the feeling says before you do."],"gemini-gemini-taurus":["At ten past eleven at night you are still on the phone, in a conversation that began at nine, with the tea gone cold and your voice low and easy. Sun and Moon both sit in Gemini, so thinking and feeling share one restless, curious channel. The Taurus Rising is what keeps it from sounding restless: a calm, warm, unhurried manner, a lovely voice, and a body that settles into a chair as if it had nowhere else to be. People think you are relaxed. You are fascinated, and it is a different thing.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, so mind and feeling use one channel and one speed, with no outside view. The Taurus Rising stands a sign away from both, so the unhurried, sensual face rarely matches the quick, curious pair behind it, and each barely sees the other. Mercury rules the doubled light and Venus the manner, which is why the words come out sounding like music. The effect is a very fast mind in a slow, pleasant body.","The gift of the easy ear. You listen as though there were all the time in the world, then answer with something that surprises the speaker. You are fluent, funny and kind, and you can calm a heated conversation just by staying in it with that unhurried voice.","A doubled Gemini will talk about a feeling in place of having one, and the Rising lends the performance a convincing calm. Nobody, including you, can tell when you are overwhelmed. Growth is noticing the body’s signals, the clenched jaw and the skipped meal, before the mind has found words for them."],"gemini-gemini-gemini":["You finish other people’s sentences, then your own in three different ways, and you usually mean all three. With Sun, Moon and Rising all in Gemini there is no gap between what you feel, what you think and what you say: it all goes straight to the tongue. You are quick, curious, funny and easy to talk to, a gallery where a remark made at one end arrives, slightly improved, at the other. What you need is not agreement but a good listener who talks back.","Three lights in one sign is total coherence and no outside view. Mercury rules all three, so need, purpose and manner trade in one currency, words, and nobody inside the house is positioned to argue with you. This is a rare ease and also a closed room: the mind explains the heart so quickly that the heart is seldom allowed to finish. Every feeling gets a name within a minute, and the name sometimes stands in for the feeling.","Fluency. You can explain, translate, joke and soothe in the same breath, and you find the link between two ideas that nobody had put together. You are tireless company, a good teacher and a natural go-between, and you make a stranger feel recently met rather than newly introduced.","When everything is talked about, nothing is allowed to be still. You can narrate a feeling so well that you never have to have it, and tire people with commentary on a mood. Growth is staying with one sensation for a full minute before naming it, and letting a friend sit quietly beside you without being entertained."],"gemini-gemini-cancer":["Three characters live in this house, and two of them share a desk. Upstairs the Gemini Sun and the Gemini Moon trade questions at speed, one wanting to know, the other wanting to say. Downstairs the Cancer Rising is taking coats, asking whether you have eaten and remembering the name of the cat. Visitors meet the host, stay for the talk and leave with a jar of something. You are warmer than you sound and chattier than you look.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, a doubled sign, so purpose and need speak the same language and rarely disagree, while the Cancer Rising stands a semi-sextile away from both, a neighbour that sees them only dimly. Because the Moon rules the Cancer Rising, the Gemini Moon runs the front door, and the hospitality itself is conversational: the kettle goes on as the questions come. The one thing the house lacks is a quiet room.","Soothing with specifics. You can calm a person by asking the right small question, then finding the words they could not find for what they were carrying. You are a natural go-between, a generous host and a letter-writer whose messages get kept.","Feelings get the same treatment as news: gathered, named and passed along. You may soothe others to avoid your own mood, or offer advice where a silence was wanted, and a house full of voices can leave no room for a quiet one. Growth is asking for one unscheduled hour at home and letting whatever turns up in it stay unexplained."],"gemini-gemini-leo":["At the head of the table you are telling the story again, and it is better than last time, because you have added a detail and a pause. The Leo Rising gives you presence: people turn toward you before you speak. Sun and Moon share Gemini, so purpose and need are one restless, curious thing that wants news, variety and an audience that talks back. You are funny, generous with attention and happiest when the room is thinking aloud.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, a doubled sign, and the Leo Rising is a sextile from both, so air and fire cooperate with unusual ease. Mercury rules the purpose and the need, and because the Sun rules your Rising, the same mind is also the chart ruler: two of the three lights are one voice, and the third is a stage for it. The difficulty is not conflict but echo. When all three enjoy talking, no light is placed to ask whether anyone is listening.","Charisma with content. You can hold a room with a story and then hand it round, ask the question that gets the shy guest talking and make a hard subject entertaining without making it small. You are a natural host, teacher and master of ceremonies.","The easy agreement between your lights can become a performance with no interval. You may fill every silence, leave a feeling before it is felt and take a quiet audience for a bad review. Growth is finishing a story without improving it, and letting one silence in the room be somebody else’s turn."],"gemini-gemini-virgo":["The world sees the calm, helpful one, the person with the pen, the plan and the spare handkerchief. The truth is that two minds are going at once. Your Gemini Sun and Gemini Moon are curious, quick and a little restless, always on the next topic and the one after. The Virgo Rising is the tidy surface laid over them, modest and observant, and it learned long ago to make the rush look like diligence. You are kinder than you let on and busier than you seem.","Mercury rules all three of your lights, so every part of you thinks, sorts and talks, and nobody inside is a different sort of creature. Sun and Moon share Gemini, a doubled sign, and the Virgo Rising stands in square to both, earth against air, so the front checks while the interior chatters. The friction is steady and domestic. Your mind rarely stops, and the manner you wear spends the day tidying up after it.","Fluent usefulness. You can listen, summarise, correct and cheer up in a single conversation, and you notice the detail that matters to the person in front of you. Anything that needs explaining you can explain, and anything that needs doing is usually next on your list.","Your nervous system lives in the mind, and the mind never rests. You can answer every message and never feel the one under it, or turn worry into another list. Good order becomes a way of not stopping. Growth is a pocket of unplanned time, kept like a handkerchief, and a feeling left unprocessed for one whole evening."],"gemini-gemini-libra":["In the week after a decision you compose both sides of the argument aloud, to whoever is nearest, and enjoy yourself very much. The Libra Rising makes you gracious, symmetrical and easy to approach, so the nearest person is usually glad. Sun and Moon share Gemini: purpose and need are one curious, talkative thing, and what you want most is a companion who answers back. Silence is allowed only as an interval. You are charming, quick and almost never alone in your own head.","All three lights are air and all three are in easy relationship: Sun and Moon in conjunction, each a trine from the Rising. That is the most fluent arrangement the wheel offers, and it has a cost. Thought, feeling and manner agree so readily that the argument between them is held in public, with a partner, rather than inside. Nothing pushes you to settle, since every position is comfortable for a while.","Fluency with grace. You can make a conversation feel like a duet, draw the shy person in and balance two points of view without losing either. You are a quick teacher, a skilled mediator and a pleasure to travel with.","With no friction anywhere, a decision can take forever. You may talk a choice round the table until it has been made by someone else, or let a feeling be explained so well that it is never felt. Growth is committing to one answer before the second opinion, and sitting in the silence that follows."],"gemini-gemini-scorpio":["When you are cornered you start asking questions, one after another, in an even voice, and each is a little closer than the last. The Scorpio Rising is why the voice is even: guarded, magnetic, a probing gaze and a charged stillness. Sun and Moon share Gemini, so purpose and need are both curious, talkative and fond of an audience. The surprise is the contrast: a mind that loves to talk behind a face that gives nothing away. People tell you things and are not sure why.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, a doubled sign, and the Scorpio Rising is a quincunx from both, sharing neither element nor mode. The two airy lights are fluent, variable and fond of the surface, while the water of the Rising is fixed, dense and private. Thought and need make the noise and the manner keeps the secret, so you can speak for an hour and have said exactly what you chose. The mind is a telegraph line running over a house with deep roots.","Penetrating fluency. You can ask the question that opens a person, listen in a way that makes them keep talking, and hold on to what they said. You are a gifted interviewer, researcher and confidant, curious enough to learn and discreet enough to be trusted.","Talking can be a way of hiding. You may give a full answer that avoids the thing asked, and ask questions in order never to be asked. People feel read and not met. Growth is answering one question as plainly as you ask them, and letting a silence be yours rather than theirs."],"gemini-gemini-sagittarius":["Three characters live in this house, and two of them are twins who have not stopped talking since breakfast. The Gemini Sun wants to know what the news is. The Gemini Moon wants someone to think aloud with, and finds stillness without ideas a kind of confinement. The Sagittarius Rising is already on the doorstep with a suitcase, laughing and wondering why nobody is coming. Visitors meet the one on the doorstep, and are carried off before they have met the others.","Sun and Moon share Gemini and the Sagittarius Rising stands opposite both: a seesaw with two lights on one end. The curious mind and the talking need agree about everything, and the manner across the wheel keeps calling them out of the room to see the world. All three are mutable, so none has the weight to hold still. The pull is between the question and the road, and the road wins most weekends.","Social velocity. You can talk to anyone in any queue, find the story in the delay and make a trip out of a week. You introduce people, answer your own questions with a laugh and collect friends across several languages.","With every light mutable, nothing holds still long enough to be finished. You may start ten threads and weave none, mistake a lot of talk for a lot of closeness, and be tired without knowing why. Growth is staying one evening in one place with one person, and letting the conversation have a single subject."],"gemini-gemini-capricorn":["With a very serious face you write small notes in the margins of a very large plan, and smile at one of them. The Capricorn Rising is composed, dry and older than the calendar, and gives you the look of someone in charge. Sun and Moon share Gemini, so purpose and need are one curious, talkative thing that wants variety, news and someone to think aloud with. The gravity is the cover. Behind it, the mind is quicker than the manner by several minutes.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, a doubled sign, and the Capricorn Rising is a quincunx from both, sharing neither element nor mode. So the two airy lights speak fast and freely, and the earthy front moves slowly and sparingly. The arrangement makes a person who thinks in several directions and acts in one. The mind is the rule and the manner is the exception, and the distance between them is where the dry humour lives.","Serious fun. You can handle a big project and enjoy the details, put a joke in a report and a plan in a joke. People find you reliable and easy to talk to, a rare pair, and you keep a hundred small things going at once without dropping them.","The poise can hide a restless mind, and the mind can hide from the poise. You may take on too much because you can, talk yourself out of rest and arrive at the end of a quarter with nothing left. Growth is saying no to one good thing, and sitting through a stretch of quiet without a notebook."],"gemini-gemini-aquarius":["People take you for the cool thinker at the edge of the room, taking notes on the species. The truth is that you are enjoying everyone, all at once, and sending messages to half of them. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance. Sun and Moon share Gemini, so purpose and need are one curious, talkative thing that wants variety, news and someone to think aloud with. The distance is a good seat for watching, and the talk is a way of coming closer.","All three lights are air, and Sun and Moon share Gemini, while the Aquarius Rising stands in trine to both: a doubled sign with an easy third. Mind, need and manner share a language and a pace. Nothing in it refuses an idea or a friend, which is its charm and its limit. A great deal of life is conducted by message, and feelings are quickly given names. The only missing voice is the one that says, stay here a minute.","Easy connection. You can talk to anyone about almost anything, introduce people who should know each other and keep a hundred friendships warm by message. You are quick, kind and strange in a way that makes others feel allowed to be.","With no friction anywhere, feeling can stay in the head. You may know the name for every mood and miss the mood, keep everyone at a pleasant range and be lonely in a very full inbox. Growth is a conversation with one person, in one room, with the phone away, for as long as it takes to say something unfinished."],"gemini-gemini-pisces":["The hour that matters is after midnight, when the day has been told and retold and the feeling behind it has not been sorted. Sun and Moon share Gemini, so purpose and need are one curious, talkative thing that wants variety, news and someone to think aloud with. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and shape-shifting, the face people project their own weather onto. You are charming, vague at the edges and slightly surprised by how much everyone tells you.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, a doubled sign, and the Pisces Rising squares both, air against water, and all three lights are mutable: nothing here holds a shape for long. The two airy lights narrate and the watery front absorbs, so you take in a great deal of weather and turn it into sentences. The friction is steady and soft: the mind keeps trying to name the mood and the manner keeps dissolving the name.","Fluent empathy. You can pick up what a person means and put it into words, listen all evening and find the sentence that helps, write a letter that makes someone cry in a good way. You are adaptable, kind and very good company.","Everything is mutable, so everything is negotiable. You may become whoever the room needs, lose track of your own preference and describe a feeling so well that you do not have to stay inside it. Growth is a decision made in one sentence and left alone, and a quiet hour with the margins empty."],"gemini-cancer-aries":["You carry it in two places: a tight, sore spot low in the stomach, and a front foot that is already moving, as if the feeling could be outrun. The Cancer Moon keeps everything: old photographs, tones of voice, the exact words said at a funeral. The Aries Rising squares it and sprints past the whole drawer, bright, direct and apparently carefree. Your Gemini Sun narrates the chase with great charm. People get the sprint. A few are shown the album.","The Cancer Moon and Aries Rising square each other, both cardinal, so what you need and how you arrive pull at right angles: the Moon wants to stay close and be held, the Rising wants to be somewhere else, first. The Gemini Sun neighbours the Moon and makes a friendly sextile to the Rising, so it is the translator, quick with words for either side and sometimes too quick to name a feeling before it has been felt. The Moon is at home in its own sign and quietly stronger than it looks.","Tenderness with momentum. You remember what matters to people and then do something about it quickly. You can make a family out of friends, tell the story of a home so vividly that strangers miss it, and be brave on behalf of anyone you have decided to protect.","Feelings are narrated rather than lived, and the Rising leaves the scene before the Moon has finished. You may be brisk with the people you most want to hold. Growth is staying in the room for the second minute, after the joke, and letting a feeling be as slow as it needs to be."],"gemini-cancer-taurus":["A library at dusk: the reading lamps coming on one by one, and outside the window the soil darkening as it rains. The Gemini Sun is the reader moving between the shelves, curious about everything and quick to say what it finds. The Cancer Moon is the drawer of old photographs in the back room, tender, protective and long-remembering. The Taurus Rising is the whole building: warm, unhurried, with a lovely voice and a chair that is always free. People settle in. Only later do they find out how much you have been keeping.","These are three neighbouring signs, Gemini, Cancer and Taurus in a row, so each light sees only the one beside it: the Rising barely meets the Sun, and the Sun barely meets the Moon’s depth. Moon and Rising are a friendly sextile, so feeling and manner cooperate, soft and homely. The Sun is the visitor in this house. Mercury asks questions, the Moon answers in feelings, Venus makes the tea, and the three seldom compare notes.","Warm intelligence. You make learning feel like being looked after, you remember the details of people’s lives and you present them back with great kindness. You are a natural teacher, host and listener, and a safe person to be curious beside.","The Moon stores and the Rising soothes, so a hurt may be tidied away behind hospitality and a clever remark. The Sun finds the story in it later. Growth is letting one real feeling interrupt the conversation, and trusting that the room will stay warm."],"gemini-cancer-gemini":["Does anyone notice that the joke came just before the tears? You keep asking it silently. The Gemini Sun and Gemini Rising are a bright, chatty front: curious, quick, a little mischievous, easy with strangers. The Cancer Moon is at home in its own sign and feels like weather, with tides of tenderness that rise and fall and want a harbour, a meal and to be remembered. Between them, wit becomes your way of keeping people close while keeping the tide private.","The Cancer Moon stands one sign past both the Gemini Sun and the Gemini Rising, a semi-sextile, so the three barely see one another: a talking mind and a feeling heart in adjoining rooms. The Moon is strong in its own sign, so the need is real and persistent, while the purpose and the manner keep turning it into a story. Mercury names and the Moon remembers. You are warmer than you sound, and quieter than you seem.","Warm wit. You can make people laugh and feel safe in the same sentence, remember what matters to them and say the kind thing lightly. You are a good host, a good letter-writer and someone others tell things to, because you receive them gently.","Humour becomes a screen, and people may take the lightness at face value and never offer the harbour you need. Moods hide inside cheerful messages until they leak out as a sudden withdrawal. Growth is saying “I need an evening in” without a punchline, and letting one person hear the sentence before the joke."],"gemini-cancer-cancer":["By fifty you will see that the calls, letters and late messages were one long sentence, and that it asked whether everyone was all right. People meet tenderness first and find the wit a little later: you remember the birthdays, bring the thing in a tin and ask after the mother. Then the Gemini Sun starts up, with quick questions, accurate gossip and small jokes placed well. The Cancer Moon makes the evening matter. You keep people, stories and objects with a history close at hand.","Moon and Rising both sit in Cancer, so the Moon rules the face it wears and the feeling needs no translation: what you show is what you need. At home in its own sign, the Moon works with no friction. The Gemini Sun, one sign over from both, is the minority voice, a curious mind in a house where the heart already holds the majority. Its habit is to narrate what the Moon is doing instead of asking what the Moon wants.","Memory with warmth. You remember what people said, what they wore and who was kind to them, and you hand it back as comfort. You write the good letter, host the long dinner and keep the family stories in working order. Others feel looked after and entertained in the same hour.","Because the Moon is at home, it needs no help to feel and a great deal to rest. You may overgive in order to be needed and keep the ledger in your head, while the Sun explains the mood instead of asking where it came from. Growth is letting someone else carry the dish, and saying one need aloud before it turns into weather."],"gemini-cancer-leo":["You want to be seen by everyone and held by one person, and both wants are real. The Leo Rising walks in lit, warm and a little grand, and people lean toward you at once. The Gemini Sun has the line ready, quick, funny and well informed about everyone’s cousins. Then the evening ends and the Cancer Moon takes over, wanting a small kitchen, a familiar voice and someone to remember what happened. The applause is the way you ask to be remembered.","Gemini, Cancer and Leo are three neighbouring signs, so your lights sit shoulder to shoulder: the Sun and the Rising meet in an easy sextile across the gap, and the Moon in between is a semi-sextile from each. The Moon is at home in Cancer and works without friction, but it stands in the middle and is rarely consulted. The Sun rules the Leo Rising, so the quick mind writes the opening lines. The Moon decides whether any of them were meant.","Warmth that remembers. You can make a crowd feel welcome and one person feel chosen, hold a story in the family for years and tell it so well that it becomes true. You are generous, loyal and funny in the same hour.","The public self gives and the private self counts. You may perform cheerfulness for a table and cry in the car, or wait to be asked what is wrong when you have not said so. Growth is telling one true thing to one person before the party, and letting the applause be the dessert rather than the meal."],"gemini-cancer-virgo":["The feeling lands in your hands first: they begin straightening a cushion, a cuff, a coat left on the wrong hook. That is the Virgo Rising at work, modest, observant, helping before it is asked. The Gemini Sun lends a quick mind that narrates, and the Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, is the tide behind both, needing to be held, fed and remembered. People feel noticed before they feel evaluated. They go home helped, and often do not realise how much was felt on their behalf.","The Cancer Moon and the Virgo Rising are in sextile, water and earth, so need and manner cooperate: care shows up as usefulness, and usefulness feels like care. The Gemini Sun is the awkward third, a square from the Rising and a semi-sextile from the Moon, close enough to talk and far from agreeing. Mercury rules both Sun and Rising, so the planet that wants new things also wants them tidy. The Moon is at home and needs only to be asked.","Practical tenderness. You remember what people like, what hurt them last time and which tin the biscuits are in, and you pass it on without making a show. You can solve the problem and hold the person in the same visit, and you make a house feel looked after.","Helping can stand in for asking. You may fix a stranger’s day while your own ache goes unmentioned, and keep a quiet tally of who noticed. Worry becomes a household chore. Growth is receiving a favour without repaying it by Friday, and saying one small need aloud before the cushion is straightened."],"gemini-cancer-libra":["A tuning fork struck on the table hums for a long time, and every glass in the room answers it faintly. That is you at a gathering. The Libra Rising takes the pitch and returns it gracefully, charming, symmetrical, considerate. Your Gemini Sun turns it into conversation. The Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, is what rings: it needs to be held, fed and remembered, and it feels each small change in the room as weather. You are the guest who notices the quiet one and the host who notices the draught.","The Cancer Moon and the Libra Rising are in square, both cardinal, water against air: the need wants a harbour and the manner wants a pleasant evening, and the two keep asking each other for something different. The Gemini Sun is a trine from the Rising and only a semi-sextile from the Moon, so it talks easily with the face and barely sees the tide. The Moon is strong in its own sign, so the feeling is real and persistent even when the manner insists on cheer.","Hospitality of the whole person. You can make a gathering feel safe and elegant at once, remember what each guest needs and offer it as a small kindness. You are good with the quiet, the nervous and the grieving, and your warmth is as dependable as your wit.","The room’s mood can become your own before you have noticed. You may keep everyone comfortable and go home depleted, or smile through a hurt so well that nobody knows to ask. Moods are given charming names. Growth is leaving a gathering when you have had enough, and saying the tide out loud."],"gemini-cancer-scorpio":["Is it safe to tell them yet? You ask it of every new friend, at every table, and you answer it slowly. The Scorpio Rising offers a still, magnetic look and a charged silence. The Gemini Sun offers a quick, funny mind that fills the gap. The Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, is the cistern: feelings run like tides, and it needs to be held, fed and remembered. Two lights are water and one is air, so what you feel is far larger than what you say.","The Cancer Moon and the Scorpio Rising are in trine, water with water, so feeling and manner understand each other without words: the face guards what the heart stores. The Gemini Sun is a semi-sextile from the Moon and a quincunx from the Rising, the one light with a different element and a different mode, so the mind chatters over the surface of a deep and agreeable quiet. The Moon is at home and works without friction.","Safe keeping. You can hold a secret, a grievance or a grandmother’s recipe for decades, and you notice who is not being heard. You listen like a person with nowhere else to be, and your loyalty is a kind of shelter. People tell you things and feel lighter.","The cistern fills, and the lid stays on. You may keep everything with great tenderness and say nothing until it is a flood, or test people before telling them. The mind explains the silence as having nothing to say. Growth is letting one cup of it out before it overflows, to someone who has already shown they can carry it."],"gemini-cancer-sagittarius":["One day you will understand that you travelled so far in order to find out what home is made of, and that the answer fits in a pocket. For now the Sagittarius Rising arrives bright and restless, laughing, full of news, and people feel invited to widen their lives. The Gemini Sun keeps the stories coming, quick and curious. The Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, wants a harbour: to be held, fed and remembered. You are the traveller who phones home and the host who writes long letters.","The Gemini Sun and the Sagittarius Rising face each other in opposition, and the Cancer Moon sits a quincunx from the Rising and a semi-sextile from the Sun, with nothing in common with the manner. Home wants roots and the manner wants a road, and the mind carries messages between them. The Moon is at home in Cancer and works without friction, which is why you can leave: the tide goes with you.","Portable warmth. You can make a strange kitchen feel like home within an hour, tell a good story over a stranger’s soup and write the letter that makes a faraway person feel remembered. You are the friend who comes back with presents and stays for the washing up.","Wanting to go and wanting to be held take turns. You may leave when you feel too held, or hold on when you most need to leave, and blame the weather. Homesickness arrives on the day of the best adventure. Growth is telling someone which one you want this week, and letting them be glad for you either way."],"gemini-cancer-capricorn":["You look like someone who needs no one, and you lie awake wondering whether everyone has eaten. The Capricorn Rising is composed, dry, a little unreachable, with a harbour wall for a face. The Gemini Sun keeps the talk quick and the jokes well timed. The Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, is the cradle inside the stone: it needs to be held, fed and remembered, and to hold in return. People meet competence. The ones who stay find the lullabies.","The Cancer Moon and the Capricorn Rising sit in opposition, home across from duty, the same axis seen from both ends: the need wants warmth and the manner wants respect, and each notices what the other is neglecting. Both are cardinal, so neither waits. The Gemini Sun is a semi-sextile from the Moon and a quincunx from the Rising, the light that shares least with either, and it carries messages across the gap in a dry voice.","Strength that shelters. You can be the one who keeps a family, a team or a house standing, and the one who remembers a birthday in the middle of a deadline. Your protection is practical, your affection is reliable and your humour is the best part of both.","Provision stands in for feeling. You may give a great deal, say you are fine and let the tide go unmentioned, then be hurt that nobody noticed. The wall that keeps others safe keeps you at a distance. Growth is saying one soft sentence aloud, to someone you trust, before the dinner is served."],"gemini-cancer-aquarius":["The feeling gathers at the base of your throat, and your hand goes to it, lightly, while you ask the other person a question. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance. The Gemini Sun supplies a quick mind that keeps the conversation moving. The Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, needs to be held, fed and remembered, and to hold in return. So the warmth is real and the approach is oblique: a message, a parcel, a porch light left on for a friend three time zones away.","The Cancer Moon sits a quincunx from the Aquarius Rising, sharing neither element nor mode: the need wants closeness and a harbour, and the manner wants room and a wide circle, and they are always adjusting to each other. The Gemini Sun is in trine with the Rising, so thought and manner talk easily, and a semi-sextile from the Moon, which it sees poorly. The Moon is at home and works without friction, but it has to be asked.","Warmth that travels. You can make a friend in another country feel remembered, bring a stranger into the circle and keep a house where odd people feel at ease. Your care is practical, your messages are well timed and your loyalty lasts.","Warmth at a distance can become a way of avoiding being held. You may keep the lamp lit for everyone and sit alone in the kitchen, give care freely and take it badly. The mind explains why you do not need anything. Growth is letting one person come in and sit down, and asking for dinner."],"gemini-cancer-pisces":["A bell under water still rings. The sound arrives slower and rounder, and it reaches further than you would expect. That is how people receive you. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and a little faraway, and the Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, runs like a tide: it needs to be held, fed and remembered, and to hold in return. Your Gemini Sun is the quick, curious voice on the surface, translating the sound into sentences.","The Cancer Moon and the Pisces Rising are in trine, water with water, so what you need and how you arrive understand one another without words and the interior is a large, warm, shared sea. The Gemini Sun is the odd one out, a square from the Rising, mutable against mutable, and a semi-sextile from the Moon. The mind has to keep finding words for a feeling that is already fluent. The Moon is at home in Cancer and works without friction.","Deep tenderness. You can hold a person without making them feel held, sense what is wrong before it is said and make a shelter out of a sentence. You remember the small things, tend them and keep them. People tell you the true story.","Two water lights take in whatever is nearby. You may mistake another person’s mood for your own, keep the household afloat and forget to ask for food, or let the mind explain that you are fine. The bell rings and nobody asks who is pulling the rope. Growth is saying, plainly, “I need to be looked after tonight,” and letting somebody do it."],"gemini-leo-aries":["The first minute at a party, when the door opens and heads turn, is your favourite minute, and you have long practised looking as though it is an accident. The Aries Rising makes the entrance direct and unhurried by doubt. The Leo Moon, in easy trine with it, needs the warmth and the applause and is wounded by being overlooked. Your Gemini Sun is already in the middle of the room, collecting stories to tell about everyone. You are good company, and a little more sensitive to the audience than you let on.","Fire holds two of your lights: Leo Moon and Aries Rising are a trine, so need and manner flow together with warmth, daring and very little self-doubt. The Gemini Sun makes a sextile to both, an easy angle, so curiosity and humour feed the blaze rather than arguing with it. It is an arc of ease, and its only weakness is that nothing in it slows down. You can be brilliant for an evening and unsure by Tuesday what you actually said.","Warmth that moves. You can charm a room, tell the story that makes it laugh and make each person feel briefly like the guest of honour. You are generous, playful and brave, and you give courage to shy people by making the first move for them.","The Moon needs to be seen and the Rising performs the seeing for it, so applause may be mistaken for contact. The Sun then gathers new material about the audience instead of about yourself. Growth is one conversation a week with no audience, in which you say what you actually need."],"gemini-leo-taurus":["Your moods are easy to read from across a room: quiet and generous when tired, theatrical when delighted, extremely polite when overlooked. The Taurus Rising gives you a calm, solid, lovely-voiced front that makes people want to sit down near you. The Leo Moon, squared to it, needs warmth, play and appreciation, and is wounded most by being overlooked. Your Gemini Sun, a friendly sextile from the Moon, writes the notes in the margin: jokes, observations, a compliment saved for later. You are better at being seen than you let on.","Leo Moon and Taurus Rising square each other, both fixed, so the need for applause and the manner of calm are stubborn companions: the Moon wants to shine, the Rising prefers to be dependable and let the work speak. The Gemini Sun makes a sextile with the Moon, so wit and warmth help each other out, and it only half hears the cautious voice of the Rising next door. The effect is a generous, funny person with a good deal of dignity to protect.","Warm, intelligent presence. You make people feel looked at, remembered and funny. You are generous with praise because you know what it is to wait for it, and the calm of the manner lets your warmth arrive without pressure. You can lead a group, a table or a classroom without raising your voice.","The Moon wants to be asked and the Rising will not beg, so you may wait for appreciation until it hardens into a polite chill. The Sun narrates the injury as an anecdote. Growth is asking for what you want, once, in your own lovely voice, and letting someone say yes."],"gemini-leo-gemini":["Think of the three lights as characters in one house. The Gemini Sun is the reporter, always at the window with the latest. The Gemini Rising is the host at the door, quick and charming, introducing everyone to everyone. The Leo Moon is upstairs rehearsing, needing warmth, play and a real audience. Downstairs the news is shared; upstairs, someone wants to be seen. You are playful, generous and a little theatrical, and an overlooked evening hurts you more than a criticised one.","The Leo Moon sits in sextile with both the Gemini Sun and the Gemini Rising, so fire feeds air: your words give the flair a stage and the flair gives the words their colour. Little in the geometry fights. The one difference is stubbornness. The Moon is fixed while the Sun and Rising are mutable, so the performer stays in character long after the mind has moved on to another topic.","Warm showmanship. You can tell a story so that a table leans in, bring play to a dull meeting and make others feel chosen for a moment. Your praise is generous and specific, and your jokes include the room rather than aim at it.","Wanting the applause can turn a conversation into a performance, and a quiet reaction can feel like a verdict. You may talk past someone who needed the stage too. Growth is asking one question whose answer you do not know, and letting the answer be the show."],"gemini-leo-cancer":["At the door you take the coats with a small bow and a joke, then glance back to see whether the joke landed. The Cancer Rising makes you attentive and careful, a host before a performer. The Gemini Sun keeps the talk quick and the stories good. The Leo Moon is the secret: a need for warmth, play and real appreciation, and its colour only shows once someone has made you feel safe. Then a carousel starts up in the cellar, and you are funnier, braver and louder than anyone expected.","The Leo Moon sits a sextile from the Gemini Sun, so wit and warmth cooperate readily: the words are what the warmth wears. The Cancer Rising is the sign between Gemini and Leo, a semi-sextile to each, and sees the Moon only dimly, which is why the shy front rarely shows how large the need is. Cancer is ruled by the Moon, so the Leo Moon is the chart ruler: what steers you is the wish to be wholeheartedly seen.","Generous warmth with manners. You make people feel noticed, and you do it with details: the toast that tells the right story, the card with the private joke, the dinner that was clearly planned for them. You are loyal in a crisis and good at making a small gathering feel like an occasion.","Being overlooked hurts most and hides best. A cancelled plan or a lukewarm reply can send you back behind the door, cheerful and wounded at once, waiting for someone to guess. Growth is asking for the attention in a plain sentence, and letting yourself be seen a little before the hurt arrives."],"gemini-leo-leo":["People think you are showing off. Mostly you are showing up: putting on the voice, the colour and the story because the evening needs somebody to start it. Leo is your Moon and your Rising, so what you need and how you arrive are one warm, proud, playful creature that wears its feelings in bright colours and wants, quite plainly, to be seen. The Gemini Sun keeps the performance quick and interesting. The crown is paper, and you know it, and you wear it anyway because it makes the room braver.","Moon and Rising share Leo, a doubled sign, so what you need and how you arrive are the same bright thing: no gap, no disguise, and a very legible hurt when the applause stops. The Sun in Gemini is a sextile from both, which gives the fire a fast, funny voice. As the Sun rules the Leo Rising, the quick mind is chart ruler and writes the lines. The warmth is coherent, and so is the vulnerability, and everyone can see where it is.","Generosity with flair. You make others feel noticed, give the compliment that is exactly true and turn an ordinary dinner into an occasion. Your feelings arrive in colour, so people know where they stand with you, and your play is infectious, quick and kind.","Being overlooked is the one wound the whole house feels at once. A flat reaction can turn a good evening into a verdict, and you may escalate the show when what you wanted was one steady pair of eyes. Growth is asking one person to look at you properly, and trusting that the look will not vanish when the room empties."],"gemini-leo-virgo":["The hour after the party is yours: plates stacked, guests gone, and a faint ache that nobody quite said the thing you were waiting to hear. The Virgo Rising is the one who stayed to clear, modest and efficient and quick to spot the cracked glass. Your Gemini Sun is the funny, quick mind that made the evening go. The Leo Moon is the secret. It needs warmth, appreciation and play, and it is wounded most by being overlooked and healed by being truly seen.","The Leo Moon is in sextile with the Sun, so wit and warmth cooperate: the words give the need its colour. The Virgo Rising is a square from the Sun and only a semi-sextile from the Moon, so the manner shuts the shutters on a need it can barely see. The result is a bonfire kept in a pharmacy, with labelled jars along the shelf. People admire the order and never see what it is guarding, and you do not always say.","Generous precision. You can find the compliment that is exactly true, plan the surprise down to the candle and make a small gathering feel cherished. Your help comes with style, your standards are warm and your play, once it is let out, is irresistible.","Being unseen hurts more than you will say. You may hide the need behind helpfulness, then feel unthanked for the favours. Modesty and pride take turns, and criticism lands as a verdict on the whole evening. Growth is asking, in one plain sentence, for the attention you want, and taking the praise without correcting it."],"gemini-leo-libra":["Hurt makes you more gracious, and the graciousness gets brighter each time. The Libra Rising makes that easy: charming, even handed, good with a seating plan and a compliment. Your Gemini Sun supplies the wit. The Leo Moon needs warmth, appreciation and play, and it is wounded most by being overlooked and healed by being truly seen. So you perform fairness with great style and quietly hope someone will notice how much it costs. The warmth is real, and so is the ache behind the cheer.","This is an arc of ease: a trine from Sun to Rising, and a sextile from each of them to the Leo Moon, with air and fire feeding one another. Thought, manner and need all cooperate, and the result is a person who is glad to be generous and sociable. Because everything flows, the one thing missing is resistance: no light is placed to refuse a request or to say the evening has gone on long enough.","Gracious warmth. You can make a whole table feel included, give praise that is specific and mean it, and carry a celebration with a very light hand. Your play is generous, your standards of courtesy are high and your loyalty is public.","Being overlooked is the one thing you will not mention. You may over give to earn the notice, then keep a bright face over the ache, and the effort goes unseen exactly because it was made to look easy. Growth is saying “I would like to be thanked” once, aloud, and letting the room hear it."],"gemini-leo-scorpio":["Inside, a house holds three residents. The Gemini Sun is in the library at dusk, reading, talking to itself and wanting everything explained. The Scorpio Rising is at the door, silent, watching who comes in and deciding whether to open it. The Leo Moon is in the attic with a lamp and a mirror, wanting warmth, play and to be seen. Visitors meet the one at the door and are not sure they were seen back.","The Leo Moon and the Scorpio Rising are both fixed and in square, fire against water: what you need is to be warmly seen, and how you arrive is guarded and hard to read. The pull between the lamp and the shutter is strong, and neither will move first. The Gemini Sun is a sextile from the Moon, so wit and warmth cooperate, and a quincunx from the Rising, so the mind is an awkward fit for the stillness. A good joke is often the key.","Warmth with weight. You can be funny and serious in the same sentence, give a compliment that is believed because you are so sparing with them and make a room fall quiet in a good way. Your loyalty is generous and deep, and your play, once it is let out, is irresistible.","Wounded by being overlooked, you may go behind the glass and let nobody know it. Pride and privacy stand guard together, and the lamp stays unlit while someone waits to be asked. The wit covers the hurt. Growth is switching the lamp on in front of one person, and asking directly for the attention you want."],"gemini-leo-sagittarius":["The news is already in your mouth when you reach the party door, a bottle in your hand and an arm round someone you met ten minutes ago. The Sagittarius Rising makes the entrance, bright, restless, laughing, inviting everyone to widen their lives. The Gemini Sun is the quick, curious mind with a story from every city. The Leo Moon is the bonfire: it needs warmth, appreciation and play, and it is wounded most by being overlooked. You are generous, loud and rarely at a loss.","The Leo Moon and the Sagittarius Rising are both fire and in trine, so what you need and how you arrive pull in one direction: more people, more colour, more light. The Gemini Sun is a sextile from the Moon, so wit and warmth cooperate, and an opposition to the Rising, so the mind keeps asking questions of a manner that already has a speech. Two mutable lights and a fixed one: the fire is steady and the talk moves.","Hospitality on a large scale. You make a stranger feel like the guest of honour, tell a story so that it includes everyone and bring play to a long journey. You are warm, funny and good at the toast.","Applause can be mistaken for connection. You may entertain a room and go home feeling unmet, or move on from a good friend because the next audience is larger. Being overlooked is the sore place, and you may talk louder when it is touched. Growth is sitting still by the fire while one person tells you their story."],"gemini-leo-capricorn":["People think you are cool, reserved and a little above applause. The truth is that the dryness is how you ask for it. The Capricorn Rising looks composed and older than the calendar, a person to be trusted with the archive. The Gemini Sun supplies the wit. The Leo Moon needs warmth, appreciation and play, and it is wounded most by being overlooked and healed by being truly seen. You are the colleague who delivers the best line in the meeting with no expression at all, then watches who laughed.","This is a yod by sign: the Gemini Sun and the Leo Moon are in easy sextile, and both stand a quincunx from the Capricorn Rising. The two warm, quick lights share nothing with the grave front, neither element nor mode. So what you are and what you need agree, and what you show is a different language altogether. All three lights differ in element and in mode, so nothing doubles and nothing backs the Moon up when it wants to be seen.","Dry warmth. You can make a serious room laugh and a shy colleague feel seen, give a compliment that people keep for years and bring colour to an ordinary agenda. You are reliable and generous, and the generosity has style.","The Moon wants applause and the Rising refuses to ask, so the need goes unspoken and the hurt goes unseen. You may overwork to be noticed, then be wounded when the notice is a nod. Growth is saying “I would like to hear what you thought”, with the face still dry and the question real."],"gemini-leo-aquarius":["The minute after you have said something brilliant and the room has moved on to the buffet is the minute that stays with you. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance, which makes you easy to admire and difficult to approach. The Gemini Sun supplies the wit. The Leo Moon needs warmth, appreciation and play, and it is wounded most by being overlooked and healed by being truly seen. You host the party, then wonder from the kitchen whether anyone noticed.","The Leo Moon and the Aquarius Rising are in opposition, both fixed: the need to be warmly seen faces the manner of friendly distance, so you offer the room your best and hold your hands out of reach. The Gemini Sun is in sextile with the Moon and trine with the Rising, so it is on good terms with both ends and carries a message across. Wit is the bridge, and a good joke is often the way the Moon asks.","Generous distance. You can be the best loved person at a gathering without making anyone feel owned, give praise that is exact and feel real joy in other people’s success. You are funny, loyal and large hearted in a way that surprises people who thought you detached.","Warmth and coolness take turns. You may withdraw the moment you most want a response, or act as though applause is beneath you while listening for it. Being overlooked hurts, and the manner will not say so. Growth is asking, once, for the attention you want, in a warm voice, and trusting the room to give it."],"gemini-leo-pisces":["Being overlooked makes you softer rather than louder, and the softness is a request. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and faraway, so people project onto you and do not always see you. The Gemini Sun supplies a quick, curious mind that keeps the conversation warm. The Leo Moon needs warmth, appreciation and play, and it is healed by being truly seen. You are a sunflower in the fog: turned toward the light, and not always easy to find in it.","The Leo Moon is a sextile from the Gemini Sun, so wit and warmth cooperate. The Pisces Rising is a square from the Sun, both mutable, and a quincunx from the Moon, sharing neither element nor mode: the gentle, blurring front and the bright, wanting heart keep adjusting to each other. The Moon asks to be seen and the Rising invites everyone to see whatever they like. Colour is how the Moon speaks, and the fog is how the Rising dresses it.","Gentle warmth. You can make a person feel their best self is being seen, play with children and elders on equal terms and make an ordinary room feel like an occasion. Your kindness is colourful, your imagination generous and your praise accurate.","The need to be seen and the habit of being gentle work against each other. You may wait to be noticed rather than ask, take the projection for the person, and feel flat when the applause is for someone else. Growth is saying, in a plain sentence, what you would like to hear, and letting the fog lift for a minute at a time."],"gemini-virgo-aries":["A shelf of apothecary jars, each labelled in a small, exact hand, and on the draining board beside them a paper boat launched on the washing-up water. That is your household. The Virgo Moon labels, sorts and worries usefully. Your Gemini Sun, ruled by the same Mercury, folds the boat, because ideas want to be tried and not only filed. The Aries Rising is the hand that knocks the jars over in its hurry to see whether the boat floats. People meet speed and bluntness. The care shows later.","Mercury rules both Sun and Moon, so thought and feeling speak a precise, quick language, yet the two signs square each other, both mutable: the Sun wants to explore, the Moon wants to get it right, and each thinks the other is dithering. The Aries Rising is a friendly sextile to the Sun and an awkward fit with the Moon, so the manner you show is bolder than the worry you hold. You are fast in public and a perfectionist in private.","Quick, careful intelligence. You can improvise and then tidy, which is why the work you hand over is both original and correct. You teach, edit, fix and explain with a directness that spares people their own confusion, and you do it with real kindness.","The Moon audits and the Rising pushes on, so criticism is turned inward at night and outward, briskly, by day. Worry is dressed as efficiency. Growth is letting a rough draft stay rough for one afternoon, and telling someone the worry before it has become a list."],"gemini-virgo-taurus":["Is that exactly true, and is it kind, and can I still say it well? You ask it before most sentences, which is why your sentences are so good. The Virgo Moon needs order, usefulness and accuracy, and worries as other people breathe. The Taurus Rising, in easy trine with it, adds calm, a lovely voice and a feeling of reliability. Your Gemini Sun, ruled by the same Mercury as the Moon, wants to say everything and say it now. The compromise is a careful speaker with a quick mind and a needle always threaded.","Mercury rules both Sun and Moon, so thought and feeling share a precise, quick language, yet the two signs square each other, both mutable: the Sun wants to explore, the Moon wants to get it right. The Taurus Rising is a trine to the Moon, so the manner supports the careful side of you with ease, while it stands a single sign from the Sun. It is a grounded arrangement, calm outside, anxious inside, and very good at repairing things.","Careful brilliance. You edit, repair and explain with accuracy and grace, you notice the flaw others miss and you tell them about it in a voice that makes it feel like help. People trust your judgement, and rightly, because you do not say what you have not checked.","The Moon audits and the Rising keeps a composed face, so worry is rarely visible and rarely shared. The Sun then talks about everything except it. Growth is saying “I am worried” in the same calm voice you use for good news, and letting someone else hold the thread."],"gemini-virgo-gemini":["Years from now you will look back and understand that the worry was a way of loving: the lists, the corrections, the emails read twice. Right now it feels like weather. The Gemini Sun and Gemini Rising are light, quick and companionable, ready to talk about anything. The Virgo Moon needs order, a task to finish and the quiet satisfaction of something done properly. So you arrive easy and leave with the checklist, charming at the party and annoyed with yourself in the car.","The Virgo Moon squares both Gemini lights, and all three are mutable, so the friction is restless rather than stubborn. One planet, Mercury, rules all three signs, which lets the voice and the nerves share a single mind. That is also why nobody inside says enough: the same speed that finds a thought finds its flaw. The Moon wants the thing right, the Sun wants the next thing, and the Rising keeps both entertained.","Precision with warmth. You can edit, repair, explain and organise, and you do it so that people feel looked after rather than corrected. You notice the missing comma and the missing friend, and you are generous with practical help.","Worry and curiosity use the same engine, so a question can turn into an inspection and a plan into a list of faults, mostly your own. You rest by switching topics, which is not the same as rest. Growth is leaving one thing good enough and sitting down before the next question arrives."],"gemini-virgo-cancer":["You are easy to talk to and hard to satisfy, and both are acts of care. The Cancer Rising welcomes: the right question, the offered chair, the memory of how someone takes their tea. The Gemini Sun is the lively mind behind it, quick to collect an idea and pass it on. The Virgo Moon is the one checking the date on the milk. It feels through doing, so a mended hem, a sorted drawer or a corrected form is how you say you were thinking of someone.","Mercury rules both your Sun and your Moon, so one planet runs the purpose and the need, but in two moods: Gemini gathers every notion, Virgo wants them filed. That is why the two are in square, both mutable and in friction, and why the evening so often turns into a tidy argument with yourself. The Virgo Moon is in sextile with the Cancer Rising, so need and welcome cooperate well: care and usefulness are one act.","Competent kindness. You notice what needs doing and do it before the helplessness is announced, and you can explain it clearly as well. You are the friend who finds the lost thing, drafts the awkward email and remembers the appointment, and you make others feel looked after without making them feel small.","Worry has a wide gate here, and care can slide into quiet correction. You may fix people, check on them or reword their sentences, then wonder why the thanks feels thin. Growth is letting something be good enough in the kitchen and in a message, and receiving a thank you without adding a footnote."],"gemini-virgo-leo":["Your shoulders rise half an inch before the nerves are admitted, and you smooth a sleeve that does not need it. That is the Leo Rising entering a room and the Virgo Moon inspecting it in the same second. The front is warm, polished and easy to watch. The need behind it is for order, use and quiet competence: the notes are in the right folder, the toast is rehearsed, the glass is not smudged. The Gemini Sun gives the talk its quickness and the worry its vocabulary.","Mercury rules both your Sun and your Moon, so one planet drives purpose and need, but in a square, mutable against mutable: Gemini wants to collect everything, Virgo wants to correct it. The Leo Rising is a sextile from the Sun and a semi-sextile from the Moon, and since the Sun rules it, the Gemini Sun is the chart ruler. The performance is loose and talkative while the private editor works overtime in the wings.","Polish with warmth. You can prepare thoroughly and still perform loosely, make a detailed plan feel like a party and a party feel like a plan. People trust your standards because you apply them kindly, and they come to you for the final edit and the first toast.","Rehearsal can turn into a way of not being seen. You may rewrite the message ten times, or take one wrong word in the toast as proof against the whole evening. Praise passes through the filter and criticism stays. Growth is releasing a thing at good enough and letting the room like it before you have found the flaw."],"gemini-virgo-virgo":["An herb garden is planted in rows because the gardener loves the plants too much to let them tangle: this one for the cough, this one for sleep, this one for the soup. Your mind works the same way. The Gemini Sun gathers cuttings from every conversation, and the Virgo Moon and Rising plant them in order, with labels in a clear hand. People meet someone modest, observant and useful. What they do not see is the gardener’s worry that something is about to go to seed.","Moon and Rising share Virgo, a doubled sign, so what you need and how you arrive are one tidy thing, and the Gemini Sun stands in square to both, air against earth. Mercury rules all three lights, so everything here thinks, files and checks. The tension is not about disagreement but about pace: the Sun wants another cutting and the earth lights want to finish the row. Feeling arrives as a to do list.","Careful brilliance. You can learn a subject and then make it usable, edit a mess into sense and notice the one error in the paragraph. Your help is concrete, your advice is specific and your quiet reliability is the reason other people can relax.","Worry is the weather, and the weather can be constant. You may fix people rather than feel with them, correct the sentence instead of hearing the sadness in it, or delay a good thing until it is ready. Growth is letting one corner of the garden grow without a label, and calling it a meadow."],"gemini-virgo-libra":["Is it fair, and is it finished? You ask both at the table, at the desk and after every kind gesture. The Libra Rising has already made things pleasant: gracious, symmetrical, attentive to the other person’s comfort. The Gemini Sun is the quick, funny mind moving through. The Virgo Moon is the one sorting the harvest in the back: it needs order, usefulness and quiet competence, and it feels through doing and fixing. People enjoy your ease. You enjoy it less than they do, until the task is done.","Mercury rules both Sun and Moon, so thought and need share a planet, yet they stand in square, mutable against mutable, the quick mind against the careful one. The Libra Rising is a trine from the Sun, which makes the surface effortless, and a semi-sextile from the Moon, so the charm barely sees the worry that keeps it in order. You are easy company and hard on your own work.","Charming competence. You can make a hard task feel pleasant and a pleasant evening run on time. You see what needs smoothing, fix it in silence and leave people better organised and more at ease. Your editing is kind, and your hosting is exact.","Nothing is quite finished enough to be given. You may weigh and revise until the moment has passed, or keep fairness and flaw finding in the same ledger. Worry is the weather behind the charm. Growth is giving the thing at ninety percent, and trusting the friend to love the rest."],"gemini-virgo-scorpio":["Looking back you will see that what you took for coldness was triage: you were sorting what could be helped from what had to be endured. For now the Scorpio Rising gives a guarded, steady gaze, and people feel read before they have said anything. The Gemini Sun asks the quick questions and makes the dry joke. The Virgo Moon feels through doing and fixing, and needs order, usefulness and quiet competence. You look at a mess, and then start on it, without comment.","The Virgo Moon is in sextile with the Scorpio Rising, earth and water, so what you need and how you arrive cooperate: the probing look and the practical hand work as one instrument. The Gemini Sun is the odd light, a quincunx from the Rising and a square from the Moon, though Mercury rules the Sun and the Moon alike, so the quick mind keeps proposing new subjects to a house that is busy with repairs. The result is thoroughness, with a joke delivered from the workbench.","Useful depth. You can look at a mess nobody else wants and find where to begin, help without drama and keep a confidence while you do it. You diagnose accurately and tell the truth in practical terms, and others are glad to have been on the receiving end.","Worry and suspicion can feed one another. You may fix people who did not ask, check the same detail several times or conclude the worst quietly and take it as evidence. A clean room can be a prayer or a shield. Growth is letting a problem sit unsolved for a day, and hearing what someone is feeling before you offer the repair."],"gemini-virgo-sagittarius":["You are the spontaneous one at the planning meeting and the organised one on the road. The Sagittarius Rising arrives bright, restless and laughing, with news, and invites everyone to come. The Gemini Sun lends a quick mind that wants to know everything about where you are going. The Virgo Moon is the sieve: it feels through doing and fixing, needs order, usefulness and quiet competence, and checks the tickets while you are telling the story.","This is a T-square by sign: Sun and Rising face each other in opposition, and the Virgo Moon squares them both, so every light is pulled by the other two and all three are mutable. Mercury rules the Sun and the Moon alike, and the quarrel between them is about pace: one collects, one sorts, and the manner across the wheel says go. A great deal of your energy is spent on logistics, which you enjoy and complain about.","Adventure with a spare charger. You can make a bold plan work, solve the problem on the platform and keep a good humour while doing it. You are the one who brings the map, the plasters and the joke.","Worry rides in the same carriage as optimism. You may check what cannot be checked, or take the leap and then fret about the landing. Criticism and enthusiasm take turns. Growth is leaving one thing unplanned, and trusting that a good day can be made from what is in your bag."],"gemini-virgo-capricorn":["Your hands go cold and your spine straightens, as if you were testing river ice with one foot, before you have found the feeling that goes with it. The Capricorn Rising is composed, serious and dry, and looks older than the calendar. The Gemini Sun supplies a quick mind that talks you across. The Virgo Moon feels through doing and fixing, and needs order, usefulness and quiet competence. The worry is a weather, and the checking is a prayer. When you step out, you cross very well.","The Virgo Moon and the Capricorn Rising are both earth and in trine, so need and manner share a taste for method, thrift and doing it properly. Mercury rules the Sun and the Moon alike, yet they sit in square, the quick mind and the careful one, and the friction is about pace. The Sun is also a quincunx from the Rising, with nothing in common, so the mind keeps being the lightest thing in a very orderly house.","Careful lightness. You can check a plan to the last detail and then explain it with a joke, repair what is broken and make it look easy. People trust your thoroughness and enjoy your company, and your work stays in good order after you leave.","Worry and duty work the same shift. You may re-check what is already right, defer rest until the list is done and be dry about your own tiredness. Feelings are filed as tasks. Growth is stepping onto the ice before it has been fully tested, and letting a mistake be an ordinary Tuesday."],"gemini-virgo-aquarius":["A blueprint drawn on glass can be corrected from either side, and the correction shows through the whole design. That is how you work. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance, a little ahead of the present. The Gemini Sun keeps the ideas coming and the notes in the margin. The Virgo Moon feels through doing and fixing, and needs order, usefulness and quiet competence. People meet the original thinker. The ones who work with you meet the person who stayed to fix the footnotes.","Mercury rules both Sun and Moon, so thought and need share a planet, yet they stand in square, the quick mind against the careful one, and the friction is about pace. The Aquarius Rising is a trine from the Sun, so mind and manner speak easily, and a quincunx from the Moon, so the need is the light that must keep adjusting. The front is open and unusual, and the need is for a tidy desk.","Useful originality. You can see a better system and then build it so that it works on a Monday. You notice the flaw, say so kindly and fix it with minimal fuss. Your work improves the people around it, and your help is concrete.","The editor never rests. You may revise a good idea until it has lost its life, or notice every error in someone else’s plan and wonder why the thanks is cool. Worry is the weather. Growth is releasing one imperfect thing into the world, and letting the friends it reaches finish it."],"gemini-virgo-pisces":["How much of this is mine to fix? You ask it in the middle of helping, with the rain already coming in. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and shape-shifting, so everyone brings you their troubles. The Gemini Sun lends a quick, curious mind that sorts them into questions. The Virgo Moon feels through doing and fixing, and needs order, usefulness and quiet competence; worry is the weather, and a clean room is a prayer. You keep the matches dry for everyone, and often forget your own.","This is a T-square by sign: the Virgo Moon and the Pisces Rising face each other across the wheel in opposition, analysis against dissolving, and the Gemini Sun squares them both, all three mutable. Mercury rules the Sun and the Moon alike, so the same planet that wants new ideas also wants them filed. The Rising invites the flood, the Moon starts to bail, and the Sun narrates both. It is a busy, kind and quite tiring arrangement.","Practical compassion. You can sense what a person needs and know the sensible next step, sit with someone in distress and find the form to fill in. You bring order to other people’s weather, with tenderness and without condescension.","Every kindness becomes a to do. You may take on more than is yours, absorb a mood and fix it as a problem, or worry in the exact shape of a list. The need to help and the need to dissolve will not share a desk. Growth is deciding what is not yours, and giving the dissolving its own hour with nothing to fix."],"gemini-libra-aries":["Boredom makes you start a debate and tiredness makes you make peace. The Aries Rising opens the conversation like a door kicked ajar: direct, quick, a little provocative. The Libra Moon, directly opposite, needs the opposite: fairness, a companion and a room with the tension gone. Your Gemini Sun, in easy trine with the Moon, enjoys both and sells each to the other. People see a sparring partner. Those who stay find a diplomat who needs the argument to end well.","Libra Moon and Aries Rising face each other across the wheel, both cardinal, so what you need and how you arrive balance on a narrow beam: harmony against initiative, we against I. The Gemini Sun is a trine to the Moon and a sextile to the Rising, so it has an easy line to both and does the translating, usually with humour. Venus wants the table settled; Mars wants to know who is right. Your skill is to be partisan and fair in the same sentence.","Persuasion with manners. You can disagree vigorously and still leave people feeling respected, argue a case from both sides and then choose one, and break an awkward silence by asking the right question. You make other people braver and more fair-minded at once.","Provocation can become a way of testing closeness, and peace-making a way of avoiding it. The Moon wants calm, the Rising wants a fight, and the Sun keeps talking. Growth is saying what you want before the debate begins, instead of discovering it in the middle."],"gemini-libra-taurus":["Three people share the salon. The Gemini Sun stands at the bookshelf reading aloud to whoever is nearest. The Libra Moon moves the cushions so that nobody is left out and the light is kind to everyone. The Taurus Rising has already put the kettle on and is gazing at the horizon, which is a degree off level and bothers nobody but the Moon. Guests find a courteous, easy, unhurried host. The household knows the Moon is quietly checking that every voice has been heard.","Two air lights and an earth Rising. Gemini Sun and Libra Moon are a trine, so thought and need run together, sociable and fair-minded, while Venus rules both Moon and Rising, which means taste, charm and comfort are all native. The Moon and Rising sit at an awkward remove, though: the Moon wants an open conversation and a balanced room, the Rising wants a stable, familiar one. The adjustments between them are the work of your life.","Gracious sociability. You can host a gathering where nobody is left out, argue both sides with kindness, and make a decision sound like a courtesy. People feel intelligent in your company and at ease, and you remember who sat where and why.","The Moon wants harmony, the Rising wants comfort, and between them the hard conversation can be postponed indefinitely. The Sun supplies a charming reason. Growth is naming a preference before asking the room for theirs, and letting the room be briefly uneasy."],"gemini-libra-gemini":["Two friends disagree, and there you are with a napkin, drawing the map of the argument: here is where she stands, here is where he stands, here is the river between. The Gemini Sun and Gemini Rising make you quick to see both sides and charming about saying so. The Libra Moon needs peace, fairness and a companion, and feels most when something is shared. You are graceful, social and fair, and uneasy whenever a guest is left out.","All three lights are air, and the Libra Moon makes a trine to both Gemini lights: the most agreeable geometry on the wheel, and the one with a cost. Conversation, ideas and balance are native to all three, so there is almost no friction to push against. Mercury rules the manner and Venus the need, so thought and tact arrive together. It flows so easily that you can go a long time without choosing.","Fair-minded charm. You can translate between people who think they disagree, find the sentence both can accept and make a quarrel feel like a conversation. You are a gracious host, a good ear and a natural editor of other people’s disputes.","Seeing both sides can stall into holding neither, and the need for peace can postpone a decision until someone else makes it. You may say yes to keep the evening smooth, then resent the evening. Growth is naming a preference first, before asking what everyone else would like, and letting the table survive it."],"gemini-libra-cancer":["You come across as the easiest guest in the world: agreeable, flexible and up for whichever plan the group chooses. The truth is a precise sense of fairness and a long memory for the times it was not kept. The Cancer Rising is warm and careful, and it makes the peace you keep look natural. The Gemini Sun brings a quick, funny mind that meets everyone, and the Libra Moon needs company and balance the way others need food. You are a crossroads where several conversations meet, and you mind when one is being run over.","The Libra Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, two airs in easy conversation, so thinking and feeling are friends and talk freely. The Cancer Rising complicates it. Moon and Rising are both cardinal and their elements clash, air against water, so the front wants to hold and shelter while the need wants to weigh and balance. Cancer Rising is ruled by the Moon, so the Libra Moon sets the tone at the door.","Even-handed warmth. You can host both sides of an argument and leave both fed, and you find the sentence that lets each person keep their dignity. Your company is easy, your instinct for the fair share is reliable, and others bring you their quarrels because you listen to the whole of them.","Peace becomes the priority and your own complaint the casualty. You give way, keep a silent score and may be surprised by how heavy it has become. The body usually knows first: a tight chest, a clenched hand under the table. Growth is stating the complaint on the first day, while it is still small enough to be a favour."],"gemini-libra-leo":["The first minute at a party is yours: within sixty seconds you have found the one guest standing alone, made two introductions and settled a small argument about parking. The Leo Rising makes the entrance, warm and a little grand, so people feel they were expected. The Gemini Sun keeps the talk moving between groups. The Libra Moon is the reason: it needs peace, fairness and company, and it feels the mood of a room in the chest before anyone names it.","These lights make an arc of ease: a trine between Sun and Moon, two airs, and a sextile from each to the fire of the Rising. Thought, need and manner cooperate, and the result is a social fluency that costs you almost nothing. The Sun rules the Leo Rising, so the quick mind is chart ruler, and its talk is the instrument that keeps the peace. The price of so much ease is that a real disagreement can feel like a malfunction.","Social grace with substance. You can connect people who should meet, defuse a tense table with one well placed question and make a stranger feel recently expected. Your company is easy, your sense of the fair share is genuine and your praise is specific.","Keeping the evening pleasant can become a full time post. You may say yes while the chest says no, smooth over what needed a hearing and leave your own side unspoken until it has gone cold. Growth is allowing one small disagreement to stay in the room until it has been heard, and finding that the party survives it."],"gemini-libra-virgo":["Tiredness shows up as bookkeeping: you start keeping score in pencil, who gave, who got, who is owed, all of it erasable and none of it spoken. The Virgo Rising is the observant, modest front, noticing the crooked chair and the guest left out. The Gemini Sun is the quick mind in conversation, and the Libra Moon needs peace, fairness and company, feeling tension in the body before it has a name. You are easy to ask for help and hard to exploit. You see more than you say, and say it pleasantly.","The Libra Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, two airs in easy conversation, so thought and need talk freely. The Virgo Rising is the difficult light: a square from the Sun, though Mercury rules them both, and a semi-sextile from the Moon, close but unconnected. The front inspects and corrects while the need softens and balances, so a fair mind is forever being proofread.","Fair minded finesse. You can see both sides, edit a quarrel into something both parties can sign and make a correction feel like a courtesy. People ask you to read the letter before they send it, and you are generous in small, specific ways.","Keeping the peace and keeping accounts can run together. You may swallow the complaint, then record it, and bring it out as a tidy list at the wrong moment. Choice is a struggle when every option has a fair case. Growth is deciding on one imperfect thing today, and saying the complaint while it is still a small one."],"gemini-libra-libra":["Three characters share this house, and two of them finish each other’s sentences. In the library the Gemini Sun reads everything and wants to hear what you think of it. At the door the Libra Rising arranges the flowers and the introductions. Upstairs the Libra Moon sets the scales at rest, wanting peace, fairness and a companion, and feeling every unkind word in the body before it is named. Guests meet the charm and the questions. You are most yourself in a pair.","Moon and Rising share Libra, a doubled sign, so what you need and how you arrive are the same thing: harmony, pleasantness, a shared table. The Gemini Sun is a trine from both, air with air, and the three lights agree on nearly everything. Venus rules the need and the manner alike, which makes this a very gracious house with no sharp objects in it. What it lacks is the friction that would force a choice, and a verdict is always one more consultation away.","Balance with company. You can listen to two people disagree and find the sentence they can both live with, make a room feel considerate and a stranger feel recently introduced. Your fairness is genuine, your taste is calm and your company is the sort people want at the table.","Weighing can become a way of waiting. You may delay a decision until the other person makes it, then agree gracefully and feel the weight of what you did not say. The scales rest, and you do not. Growth is choosing before you have consulted everyone, and letting the choice be slightly unfair to someone for a day."],"gemini-libra-scorpio":["A pleasant question at the edge of the group, and eye contact held one second longer than anyone expected: that is how people first meet you. The Scorpio Rising supplies the second: magnetic, guarded, a probing gaze with a charged stillness. The Gemini Sun is the quick mind behind the question. The Libra Moon needs peace, fairness and a companion, and feels tension in the body before it has a name. So the inquiry is gracious, and the gaze is not. People leave feeling understood and a little unsure what they told you.","The Libra Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, air with air, so thought and need talk easily and the questions come with charm. The Scorpio Rising is a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour that cannot see it, and a quincunx from the Sun, which shares nothing with it. Peace and probing sit in the same face. The result is a fair and watchful presence that is rarely hostile and never quite relaxed.","Gracious penetration. You can ask a hard question so pleasantly that it is answered, spot what is being left out and mediate a dispute without picking a side. Your company is calm, your instincts about people are good and your discretion is solid.","The pleasantness can be a screen for the watching. You may collect information about people and hold your own back, keep the peace while privately drawing conclusions, and be hurt when others do the same. Growth is telling one person what you actually saw, kindly and aloud, and letting them answer."],"gemini-libra-sagittarius":["To most eyes you are the easy one, with no preferences and a seat for everyone. The truth is a very particular sense of who has had a turn. The Sagittarius Rising arrives bright, restless and laughing, with news, and people feel invited to widen their lives. Your Gemini Sun keeps the talk moving and the stories fair. The Libra Moon needs peace, fairness and a companion, and feels tension in the body before it is named. You tell the best story of the night, then pass the fire.","The Libra Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, air with air, and in sextile with the Sagittarius Rising, so the need is friendly to both mind and manner. The Sun and the Rising stand in opposition: asking and telling across the wheel. Libra is the mediator between them, which is the job you keep being handed at parties. The geometry is kind, and it leaves you very good at balancing and a little slow to choose.","Generous fairness. You can include the quiet one, keep the peace without silencing the loud one and tell a story so that everyone listens and no one feels lectured. You are a good travelling companion, and your talk is easy and bright.","Keeping the circle even can become a reason never to pick a side. You may smooth a disagreement you should have had, or go along with an itinerary and resent it. Tension sits in the body until it is named. Growth is stating a preference before the group has chosen, and letting the evening go in your direction for once."],"gemini-libra-capricorn":["The hour before a decision you lay the options out like a shuffled deck and find that every one of them is fair. The Capricorn Rising is composed, dry humoured and serious, and holds the ridge steadily. The Gemini Sun keeps the conversation light and well informed. The Libra Moon needs peace, fairness and a companion, and it feels tension in the body before it has a name. So you appear unbothered while a delicate balance is being kept. Silk on a cool floor, a goat on a ridge.","The Libra Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, air with air, so mind and need talk easily. The Capricorn Rising is a square from the Moon, both cardinal, earth against air: the need wants harmony and the manner wants results, and each is mildly disappointed in the other. It is also a quincunx from the Sun, so the mind never quite finds the register for it. Peace and authority share your face, and neither is quite comfortable.","Poised fairness. You can hold a position with grace, mediate between two senior people without losing either’s respect and make a difficult decision feel reasonable. You are good at tact, at structure and at being dryly funny about both.","Composure can become a way of putting off the unpleasant truth. You may weigh and re-weigh, keep the peace at the cost of a complaint and show a serene face while the body clenches. Growth is stating one preference plainly before the meeting begins, and letting the peace be a little less perfect."],"gemini-libra-aquarius":["Cornered, you become reasonable, and it works, because you are. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance. The Gemini Sun lends a quick mind that introduces everyone to everyone. The Libra Moon needs peace, fairness and a companion, and it feels tension in the body before it is named. All three lights are air, so thought, need and manner share an easy climate: you hear a whispered rumour, weigh it fairly and redraw the plan so that no one is left out.","This is a grand trine by sign: Sun, Moon and Rising are all air and each is in trine with the other two, a closed circuit of ease, with every modality different. Everything flows, and nothing presses. It is an agreeable arrangement, and it has no outside view: nobody in the circuit is placed to say that fairness is not the same as courage.","Fair minded flow. You can bring different people together and keep the conversation easy, notice who is left out and make room, and settle a disagreement with a plan both sides can sign. You are kind, social and good at the long view of a relationship.","When nothing resists, nothing pushes you to choose. You may let a decision float, say yes to keep the evening smooth and draw a perfect plan that nobody builds. The body notices the tension before you do. Growth is picking one side of a question on purpose, and saying so while the room is still friendly."],"gemini-libra-pisces":["A house, three residents, one front door. The Gemini Sun is in the kitchen with the news, delighted to tell you all of it. The Pisces Rising is in the hall, gentle and faraway, holding a lantern in the rain and letting everyone project onto it. The Libra Moon is in the courtyard with the scales at rest, wanting peace, fairness and a companion, and feeling tension in the body before it is named. Visitors come for the kitchen, stay for the hall and find their peace in the courtyard.","The Libra Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, air with air, so need and mind talk fluently. The Pisces Rising is a square from the Sun, both mutable, and a quincunx from the Moon, sharing neither element nor mode, so the soft, receptive manner is the least aligned of your lights. It takes in what the Moon wants to balance and what the Sun wants to explain. The shape is easy at the heart and shifting at the edge.","Peaceable range. You can make a gathering feel considerate, find the thing to say that will let a quarrel end and sense who needs a chair. Your manner is soft, your fairness is real and your company is easy. You are a good host, listener and mediator.","Peace can be a place to hide. You may agree with every side, absorb the tension and carry it home in the chest, and let your own preference blur. Others project calm onto you, and you provide it long after you are depleted. Growth is naming a preference at the start of an evening, and leaving before the courtyard empties you."],"gemini-scorpio-aries":["How much of this can I say out loud, and who has earned the rest? You ask it constantly, usually mid-sentence. The Gemini Sun and the Aries Rising talk and move at the same easy speed, so you look open, quick and funny. The Scorpio Moon is the courtyard behind the front gate: private, intense, and remembering every word ever said in it. Nobody who hears you talk for an hour suspects how much has been kept back. It is a very particular kind of tact, and it is not deceit.","This is a yod by sign: Gemini Sun and Aries Rising make a friendly sextile, and both stand at an awkward remove from the Scorpio Moon, which sits at the point of the figure. The Moon is therefore the light that cannot be translated into the other two, the one that needs trust, privacy and truth while the others need speed and conversation. Mars rules both Moon and Rising, so the intensity leaks into the manner as heat. The Moon is in its fall, learning through humility.","Charm with depth. You can talk easily to anyone and be trusted by a few completely. You notice what a person avoids saying, you remember the one sentence that mattered, and you can be both the life of the party and the one who sits up with someone at three in the morning.","Easy talk becomes a screen, and the real feeling is kept like a coin in a closed hand. The Rising acts before the Moon has decided, and the Moon files the consequences. Growth is telling one person, early and plainly, what the quiet part of you is holding."],"gemini-scorpio-taurus":["By fifty you will understand that the calm you wore was a vessel, and that the explaining you did was a wire strung to whatever was inside it. The Taurus Rising gives you a low, unhurried voice and a body that settles the room. The Scorpio Moon, directly opposite, feels totally or not at all, and keeps a record that never fades. Your Gemini Sun stands between, a messenger sending signals across the gap: questions, jokes, theories, a long careful letter. People think you are easy-going. A few know you are keeping the midnight hour.","Scorpio Moon and Taurus Rising face each other across the wheel, both fixed, so need and manner balance on a long beam: calm and comfort on the outside, intensity and truth on the inside, and neither will give way. The Gemini Sun sits at an awkward remove from the Moon and a sign from the Rising, so it is the go-between, curious about the whole arrangement and a little baffled by it. The Moon is in its fall, learning strength through humility.","Calm that has depth. You can sit with an enormous feeling and not flinch, ask the question that opens the hidden thing, and keep a confidence for life. In a crisis you are slow to panic, quick to understand and unusually loyal, and you speak with the voice of someone who has thought it through.","The Rising keeps the surface warm and the Moon keeps the account, so a hurt can be filed politely and held for years. The Sun explains it away cleverly and the matter stays put. Growth is saying “that cost me something” in the first week, in the plain, kind voice you already have."],"gemini-scorpio-gemini":["The most talkative guest at the party is also one of the most private. Both are true. The Gemini Sun and Gemini Rising talk easily, ask questions and share what they know, so people assume they have met all of you. The Scorpio Moon feels totally or not at all, needs trust and truth, and keeps the door to the real rooms locked. A hundred acquaintances know your jokes, and two people know where you keep the key.","The Scorpio Moon is a quincunx to both Gemini lights: five signs away, with no shared element and no shared mode. The Sun and Rising are air and mutable, the Moon water and fixed. The Moon is in its fall, so safe feeling is learned through humility, and trust comes by being shown slowly rather than argued into. The manner scatters while the need concentrates, and you shuttle between the two without a map.","Depth under good manners. You can ask a light question and hear the heavy answer, keep a secret for decades and see through a performance in a sentence. Once you trust someone, your loyalty is total and your attention is exact.","Talking to everyone can be a way of never being asked in private, and you may test people instead of telling them what you need. A hurt can be remembered for years while the face stays pleasant. Growth is saying one true sentence in a plain voice before the feeling hardens into a decision."],"gemini-scorpio-cancer":["The feeling lands in your jaw first. By the time it reaches your mouth it has become something light, and you stand with your weight on one foot, smiling, waiting to see whether it passes or is asked about. People meet the Cancer Rising, warm and attentive, and the Gemini Sun, quick and amusing. Few see the Scorpio Moon behind both, which feels totally or not at all and remembers everything. Your small talk is real, and it is also a vault door painted to look like a hallway.","Two of your lights are water and sit in an easy trine, the Cancer Rising and the Scorpio Moon, so feeling and front already share depth and privacy. The Gemini Sun is the odd one out, a quincunx from the Moon with neither element nor mode in common, so mind and need keep adjusting to each other and never quite settle. The Moon in Scorpio is in fall, and its strength is hard-won, built through humility rather than control.","Discretion with fluency. You can hear what is behind a sentence, say the right thing lightly, and keep a secret so well that others forget you are keeping it. Your loyalty is total once given. People come to you with the thing they cannot tell anyone and find they can finally say it.","Silence is your protection and can harden into a verdict. You may test people quietly instead of asking them, and let the mind explain why you are fine. A hurt that is not spoken does not fade here; it turns into distance. Growth is saying a half sentence aloud while it is still soft, to someone who has earned it."],"gemini-scorpio-leo":["In an eclipse the bright thing is not put out. It is covered, exactly, and the rim goes on blazing round the edge. That is your arrangement. The Leo Rising stands in full light, warm and magnetic, and the Gemini Sun keeps the conversation quick and amusing. The Scorpio Moon sits across the middle, feeling totally or not at all, remembering everything and showing very little. People see the corona and enjoy it. The few who wait out the dark find what was behind it.","Moon and Rising are both fixed and in square, water against fire, so what you show and what you need pull apart and neither will give way. The Moon in Scorpio is in fall, and its strength is built through humility rather than command. The Sun in Gemini is a quincunx from the Moon, sharing neither element nor mode, and spends years adjusting its questions to a heart that answers in silence. Because it rules the Leo Rising, the quick mind does the talking for all three.","Charm with weight in it. You can be the life of the evening and notice who is lying, who is lonely and who needs rescuing, all in a lit room with a good joke. People bring you what they cannot tell anyone else. Your loyalty is total once earned.","Control is the temptation. You may stage your warmth while the Moon keeps score, test people by what they fail to notice, or let a hurt harden into a very polite silence. Pride and privacy then guard the same door. Growth is letting one person see you when you are not on, and saying the hurt before it becomes a verdict."],"gemini-scorpio-virgo":["What does this person actually want, and why am I being so helpful about it? You ask it quietly, in the middle of a favour. The Virgo Rising notices everything first, modest and exact. The Gemini Sun turns the noticing into a witty remark. The Scorpio Moon is what keeps the file: it feels totally or not at all, needs trust and privacy, and remembers each detail long after the others have forgotten. You seem helpful and a little dry. People who earn your trust learn there is a well under the desk.","The Scorpio Moon is a sextile from the Virgo Rising, water and earth working together, so your depth has a competent, practical way of walking about in the world. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from the Moon and a square from the Rising: mind and need share nothing, and mind and manner share a ruling planet but not a pace. The Moon is in fall, so its strength is built through humility rather than control.","Discernment with discretion. You see the detail that gives the game away, keep a confidence without effort and find the practical help that a hurt person did not know they could ask for. You are a fine investigator, a faithful friend and someone whose silence can be relied on.","Suspicion can pose as diligence. You may check and test and file, and reach a verdict before the person has had a chance to answer. A hurt that is not told hardens into silence. Growth is asking the question aloud while it is still a question, and letting one person read the file."],"gemini-scorpio-libra":["At fifty you will see that you were never being polite to avoid the truth. You were being polite to guard the one door you were not ready to open. For now the Libra Rising offers charm, symmetry and a perfectly judged question, and the Gemini Sun turns it into good talk. The Scorpio Moon is the keyhole: it feels totally or not at all, needs trust, privacy and truth, and remembers everything. Few people are let in, and they are told the whole story.","The Scorpio Moon is in fall, so its strength is built through humility and is slow to arrive. It sits one sign from the Libra Rising, a semi-sextile, and the two barely see each other: pleasantness in front, intensity behind, neighbours with a shared wall. The Gemini Sun is a trine from the Rising and a quincunx from the Moon, so it talks easily to the face and has to learn the language of the depths from scratch.","Charm that keeps secrets. You can be easy company and a vault in the same sentence, spot what is not being said and ask the question that opens it politely. Your loyalty is deep and your tact is exact. People tell you things.","Courtesy can harden into a closed shutter. You may test people instead of asking, hold a grievance behind a pleasant face and go silent when trust is broken. The peace is real, and the verdict is already written. Growth is saying the unwelcome sentence while the feeling is still warm, and letting one person see the key."],"gemini-scorpio-scorpio":["You talk constantly and tell almost nobody anything, and both are on purpose. The Gemini Sun supplies the fluency: quick, curious, funny, fond of a good exchange. The Scorpio Moon and Scorpio Rising are the lock. They feel totally or not at all, need trust, privacy and truth, and remember everything, and they present as a still, charged gaze that people feel as being read. Your conversation is a door held open on a corridor with many more doors. The keys are on a chain, and few people have the chain.","Moon and Rising share Scorpio, a doubled sign, so what you need and how you arrive are the same: private, total and watchful. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from both, sharing neither element nor mode, so the mind is permanently a visitor in its own house, fluent in a language the household barely speaks. The Moon is in fall, and its strength is hard won, built through humility rather than control. Two lights guard and one explains.","Discreet fluency. You can talk about anything and reveal exactly what you choose, and read a room within a minute. Your loyalty is total, your memory is exact and your trust, when given, is deep. You are a formidable friend and a restful confidant.","Because the mind can talk, it can hide. You may answer every question and let nobody in, remember a betrayal for decades and keep the hurt as a verdict in silence. The Moon is in fall and has to learn humility, which is slow. Growth is handing one key to one person, and bearing the risk."],"gemini-scorpio-sagittarius":["The feeling sets in your sternum, your breath goes shallow, and you smile and tell the story anyway, a little faster. The Sagittarius Rising is the laughing, open face, bright and restless, full of news. Your Gemini Sun supplies the stories and the questions. The Scorpio Moon is the suitcase with the lock: it feels totally or not at all, needs trust, privacy and truth, and remembers everything. People think you hold nothing back. A few know there is a case you carry yourself.","The Scorpio Moon is in fall, and its strength is built through humility. It sits one sign from the Sagittarius Rising, a semi-sextile, so the two neighbours see each other poorly: openness on the front step and privacy in the hall. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from the Moon and an opposition to the Rising, so the mind swings between a heart that keeps and a manner that tells. Both are fluent. Only one has the key.","Candid depth. You can be funny about hard things, trusted with a secret by a crowd and a dependable friend on the dark days. You know when someone is not telling you the truth, and you do not make them feel caught.","The easy face can mislead people about how much is held back. You may share a hundred stories and never the one that matters, then be hurt that nobody asked. Betrayal does not fade here; it becomes a silence. Growth is saying the unwelcome sentence at the first small hurt, and letting one person carry the case with you."],"gemini-scorpio-capricorn":["River ice looks like a floor and carries a current under it, which does not stop for the winter. That is the arrangement. The Capricorn Rising is composed, dry and serious, a face that has been to the meeting already. The Gemini Sun lends a quick mind skating across the surface. The Scorpio Moon is the current: it feels totally or not at all, needs trust, privacy and truth, and remembers everything. People cross the surface with confidence. The few who stand still long enough hear the water.","This is a yod by sign: the Scorpio Moon and the Capricorn Rising are in sextile, water and earth working as partners, and the Gemini Sun is a quincunx from both. The deep need and the sober manner understand each other without words, while the quick mind shares neither element nor mode with either and has to translate. The Moon is in fall, so its strength is hard won, and the sober front helps it grow slowly and keep its own counsel.","Quiet power. You can carry a great deal without showing it, read a situation in a minute and keep faith with what you promised, whatever the weather. Your humour is dry, your word is good and your loyalty is not for sale.","The ice is thick enough to hide a lot. You may mistake control for strength, hold a hurt until it has become a policy and let others think you are fine. Betrayal hardens into silence, which looks like calm. Growth is cracking the surface for one person, on purpose, and letting the water show."],"gemini-scorpio-aquarius":["Who can I tell, and what will it cost me if I am wrong about them? You ask it in the middle of a perfectly friendly evening. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance, so people think they know your range. The Gemini Sun is the quick mind that fills every silence with something interesting. The Scorpio Moon feels totally or not at all, needs trust, privacy and truth, and remembers everything. The tower is open to visitors. The observatory has a lock, and the key is on a chain.","The Scorpio Moon and the Aquarius Rising are both fixed and in square, water against air: the need wants depth and privacy and the manner offers breadth and friendliness, and neither will give way. The Moon is in fall, so its strength is built through humility and arrives slowly. The Gemini Sun is a trine from the Rising, so mind and manner talk easily, and a quincunx from the Moon, which shares nothing with it. The result is a sociable surface over a very private room.","Depth with range. You can know a great many people and keep a few secrets for decades, read a room with a cool eye and then stand loyally beside someone in trouble. Your friendship is selective and total, and your discretion is excellent.","Friendly distance can hide a locked door. You may test people quietly, take a small betrayal as a large verdict and let the silence set like concrete. The mind explains that you are simply independent. Growth is saying the unwelcome sentence while it is still small, and handing one person the key."],"gemini-scorpio-pisces":["Late in life you will understand that you did not need so many names for what you felt. You needed one listener. For now the Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and faraway, and people project onto it freely. The Gemini Sun supplies the words. The Scorpio Moon feels totally or not at all, needs trust, privacy and truth, and remembers everything. The notes in the margin are for the world. The sealed letter is for one person, and it holds more weather than anyone knows.","The Scorpio Moon and the Pisces Rising are in trine, water with water, so the Moon and the Rising understand each other without speaking: the softness is a screen and the depth is the room behind it. The Moon is in fall, so its strength is built through humility. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from the Moon and a square from the Rising, the only airy light in a watery house, and it spends its life translating for two lights that do not need translating.","Deep reception. You can hold a secret and a sorrow without a ripple, read the room behind the room and respond in a way that heals rather than exposes. Your loyalty is quiet and total, your language is precise and your presence is unthreatening. People tell you the truth.","Softness at the surface and silence below it can combine into withdrawal. You may be hurt and call it tiredness, test someone by saying nothing, or let a betrayal harden into a very gentle distance. Growth is opening one letter on purpose, in the same hour as the hurt."],"gemini-sagittarius-aries":["Three travellers meet at a crossroads. The Gemini Sun reads every signpost aloud, with variations. The Sagittarius Moon has already chosen a direction, on faith, and is whistling. The Aries Rising has run ahead to check that the road is any good and will be back with a report, a blister and an opinion. Nobody in this party is afraid of the open road. The only quarrel is over whether to stop and read the map or simply go.","Gemini Sun and Sagittarius Moon face each other across the wheel, both mutable, so what you are and what you need are two halves of one curiosity: the particular and the whole, the question and the belief. The Aries Rising is a trine to the Moon and a sextile to the Sun, so the manner supports both with energy and courage. Two fire lights keep the chart warm and the air Sun keeps it talking. It is a lively arrangement with very little caution in it.","Contagious optimism. You make learning feel like an adventure, you encourage people to try the thing they were afraid of, and you tell the story of the trip so well that others want to go. You are brave, funny, generous with ideas and hard to discourage.","With the Sun curious, the Moon hopeful and the Rising ready, there is no brake. Plans are made faster than they can be kept, and honesty arrives as bluntness. Growth is writing down the cost of the next promise before making it, and finishing one trip before booking the next."],"gemini-sagittarius-taurus":["Between two open doors, one to the orchard and one to the road, you hold a map whose edges nobody has labelled. The Taurus Rising is the orchard: calm, solid, unhurried, with a lovely voice and a September sweetness that makes people stay. The Sagittarius Moon is the road, needing space, adventure and faith in tomorrow. Your Gemini Sun, directly opposite the Moon, wants to know about both and be on first-name terms with each. You are an easy host with a packed bag in the hall.","Gemini Sun and Sagittarius Moon face each other across the wheel, both mutable, so what you are and what you need are two halves of one curiosity: the detail and the horizon. The Taurus Rising stands a sign from the Sun and at an awkward remove from the Moon, so the stay-put manner you wear sits uneasily over a need to roam. That is why you may seem more settled than you feel. The Sun carries the argument by talking about both.","Rooted curiosity. You bring home stories, recipes, words and strangers and you make them part of the household. You are sociable, optimistic, calm in a crisis and good at making an unfamiliar place feel inviting. People trust you with both their secrets and their travel plans.","The Rising promises to stay and the Moon plans to leave, and the Sun keeps both versions of the story going. Others may feel misled when the packed bag finally leaves the hall. Growth is telling the people you love, early, which door you are looking at today."],"gemini-sagittarius-gemini":["People tend to think you collect ideas the way others collect postcards: lightly, quickly, from everywhere, with no plan to stay. The truth is that you are searching, and every conversation is a small expedition. Your Gemini Sun asks for the detail, your Gemini Rising makes the asking look like play, and the Sagittarius Moon, directly across the wheel, wants the whole horizon and a reason to believe in next year. You seem scattered and are in fact moving toward something.","The Sun and Rising face the Moon across the wheel in an opposition, and all three signs are mutable, so this is a seesaw with nobody holding the ground. Gemini wants the facts and Sagittarius the meaning, the detail and the view. Mercury and Jupiter rule the two sides, and neither wins. You feel most whole when a trip, a book or a long conversation lets both lean on each other.","Curious faith. You can gather facts and then ask what they are for, make a joke carry a belief and make a belief sound like an invitation. You are optimistic without being naive, a good travelling companion and a teacher whose lessons arrive as stories.","The seesaw can keep you in the air: facts without conviction in one hour, conviction without facts in the next. Promises are made in the Moon’s enthusiasm and kept by nobody’s patience. Growth is choosing one question to follow for a year, and letting some doors stay closed."],"gemini-sagittarius-cancer":["The hour that matters is the one before you leave: the bag is packed, the kettle is on, and you have found three reasons to stay and four to go. People meet the Cancer Rising, who feeds them and asks about their mother. They also meet the Gemini Sun, who has a story from every city. The Sagittarius Moon sets the pace: a need for space, adventure and faith in next year, with a cheerful, philosophical temper that hates a fence.","Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel in opposition, Gemini asking and Sagittarius answering, so you swing between the detail and the horizon like a seesaw. Cancer Rising is ruled by the Moon, so the Sagittarius Moon holds the keys to the house: the welcome is real, and the door is always a little ajar. The quincunx between Moon and Rising adds a tug of its own, since home wants roots and the Moon wants a road.","You bring the world home. You tell stories from elsewhere in a kitchen that makes the listener feel safe, and you make travel sound possible and returning sound welcome. You are generous with hospitality, quick with a laugh and good at making a stranger feel like a guest rather than a delay.","You are pulled two ways: wanting someone to come home to and hating to be held. You may promise a visit and cancel it, or settle in and itch. Others read the mixed signal as unreliability. Growth is building a home with windows in it, and saying “I will be back on Thursday” and being back on Thursday."],"gemini-sagittarius-leo":["Delight makes you turn the volume up and widen the guest list. When you are cornered you reach for a joke and a bigger picture. The Leo Rising brings the sunny entrance, the open arms, the sense that something good is about to happen. Your Gemini Sun has read a little of everything and wants to compare notes. The Sagittarius Moon needs space, adventure and faith in tomorrow, and it hates a fence in any language. You are generous, entertaining and rarely in the same place for long.","Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel in opposition: the Gemini habit of asking and the Sagittarius habit of answering swing like a seesaw, curiosity against conviction. The Leo Rising is a sextile from the Sun and a trine from the Moon, so both ends are fed by the same fire and the performance comes easily. The Sun rules the Rising, which makes the questioning mind chart ruler, and every time it settles on an answer the Moon shrugs and heads for the horizon.","Infectious optimism with sources. You can make a stranger feel that next year will be better and back it up with a book and a travel story. You teach by enthusiasm, forgive quickly and are very hard to depress for long.","The big picture can become a way of leaving. You promise a great deal, enjoy the promising and are surprised when someone holds you to it. Candour arrives with a laugh and sometimes lands as carelessness. Growth is choosing one commitment that has a date on it, and keeping it as if it were an adventure."],"gemini-sagittarius-virgo":["Your house has three residents, and each wants something different. The Gemini Sun sits at the window with a map and a question. The Virgo Rising is at the table sorting receipts and correcting the date on the map. The Sagittarius Moon is by the door with its bag, wanting space, adventure and a reason to believe in next year. Visitors meet the one at the table, who is helpful and exact, and are surprised by a laugh from the doorway.","This is a T-square by sign: Sun and Moon face each other in opposition, and the Virgo Rising squares them both, so every light is pulled by another, and since all three are mutable, none of them holds still. The Sun asks, the Moon answers and the Rising checks the facts. Mercury rules the Sun and the Rising, which means the quarrel is conducted in complete sentences.","Curious thoroughness. You can go on a journey and come home with a notebook, a plan and a good story. You make a trip into a lesson and a lesson into a trip. You are helpful, entertaining and honest, a combination that turns strangers into friends on a platform.","Pulled three ways, you can overload the schedule and then apologise for the pace. You may plan an adventure so thoroughly that it stops being one, or keep the door open in order never to commit. Criticism and optimism take turns. Growth is picking one of the three pulls each week and letting it lead."],"gemini-sagittarius-libra":["One foot in the room and one in the open air, on the balcony at the party, you ask a stranger where they would go if nothing were in the way. The Libra Rising is why the stranger answers: gracious, symmetrical, considerate. Your Gemini Sun has the follow up question. The Sagittarius Moon needs space, adventure and faith in tomorrow, and it hates being fenced in by a charming plan. You collect stories and people. You make leaving feel like a courtesy.","Sun and Moon are in opposition, Gemini asking and Sagittarius answering, so you swing between the detail and the horizon. The Libra Rising stands in trine to the Sun and in sextile to the Moon, and so is friendly to both ends of the seesaw: the manner can hold either conversation. That ease is a gift and a trap. Nothing in the geometry forces you to choose a library or a road, so you may keep both open for years.","Charming breadth. You can ask the question that lights a stranger up, make a plan sound like an adventure and a departure sound like a gift. Your optimism is real, your manners are lovely and your stories travel well.","You can mistake an open door for freedom. You may offer to come and not come, agree to the plan while eyeing the exit, or spread yourself charmingly and thinly. People feel liked and not known. Growth is picking one place and one person, and staying for the second visit."],"gemini-sagittarius-scorpio":["The stare gets mistaken for gravity. Mostly it is you thinking, and often it is you trying not to laugh. The Scorpio Rising gives the gaze, guarded and magnetic, and a stillness that unsettles strangers. The Gemini Sun is the quick, curious mind behind it. The Sagittarius Moon is the true weather: cheerful, philosophical, needing space, adventure and faith in tomorrow. It hates a fence, and the Rising is a very good one. Those who get past the doors find the funniest company in the building.","Sun and Moon are in opposition, Gemini against Sagittarius, the habit of asking against the habit of answering. The Scorpio Rising sits a quincunx from the Sun and a semi-sextile from the Moon: it shares a neighbourly wall with the Moon and nothing at all with the mind. The result is a seesaw with a guard at one end. The Moon wants an open road and the manner is a heavy door, and the mind keeps writing notes and passing them under it.","Depth with lightness. You can discuss something serious and make it funny without making it small, read a person’s motives and still wish them well. Your optimism has been tested and it survived, which makes it believable. You travel well, and you are good company for anyone in trouble.","The guard and the traveller work against each other. You may leap before the look and then retreat behind the door, or give a long speech while keeping the only true sentence back. Candour and secrecy take turns. Growth is picking a person to be plainly cheerful with, and letting the stare relax first."],"gemini-sagittarius-sagittarius":["The week after you decide to go is your happiest: the map is spread on the table, the edges are unlabelled, and nobody has yet asked you to be specific. Moon and Rising share Sagittarius, so need and manner are one bright, restless, laughing thing that wants space, adventure and faith in tomorrow. The Gemini Sun stands across the wheel with the notebook, curious about every village on the way. You arrive with news, leave with stories and are very hard to fence.","Moon and Rising share Sagittarius, and the Gemini Sun stands opposite both, which makes a seesaw with two lights on one end: the need and the manner lean toward the horizon, and the mind pulls back toward the detail. All three are mutable, and none holds still. The detail is not a rival; it is the notebook that makes the journey tellable. Jupiter rules the two heavy lights, so the generosity is large and the schedule is loose.","Joyful range. You can talk to any stranger, laugh at your own mistakes and make a trip, a lecture or a lunch feel like an invitation. You are generous with time, quick to forgive and good at the first week of anything.","Two lights lean forward and one takes the notes, so things are started more often than they are finished. You may promise more than you can hold and confuse movement with progress. Candour can arrive as a joke at the wrong moment. Growth is making one commitment that lasts through the boring part, and letting the notebook have the last word."],"gemini-sagittarius-capricorn":["When you are delighted you let the dry face slip and laugh out loud, and then look round to see who saw. The Capricorn Rising is composed, serious and a little older than the calendar. The Gemini Sun is the curious mind that asks the next question. The Sagittarius Moon needs space, adventure and faith in tomorrow, and it hates a fence, including the ones you build yourself. The manner is a high wall around a quiet courtyard, and the laughter comes over the top.","Sun and Moon face each other in opposition, Gemini asking and Sagittarius answering, and the Capricorn Rising is a quincunx from the Sun and a semi-sextile from the Moon, so it sees the Moon poorly and the mind not at all. The arrangement is a seesaw with a stern attendant. The Moon wants the leap and the Rising wants the plan, and the Sun writes a good argument for both.","Serious optimism. You can hold a plan and a hope at once, tell a story with a straight face and a gleam, and make a long road feel like a good idea. Your word is kept, your laughter is generous and your faith has been tested.","The leap and the ledger take turns. You may promise a journey and then bury it under duty, or break loose and leave the work undone. The dry face hides how much the Moon wants out. Growth is scheduling one thing for the joy of it, and not apologising for it."],"gemini-sagittarius-aquarius":["Picture a house with three residents, each convinced the others have the wrong idea. The Gemini Sun sits at the desk with a notebook, writing questions in the margins. The Aquarius Rising stands in the hall with a coat on, cool, friendly and slightly ahead of schedule. The Sagittarius Moon is at the garden door, wanting space, adventure and faith in tomorrow, and wondering why anyone would sit indoors during a storm with the window open. Guests find the one in the hall easy to talk to, and are surprised how fast the other two get out.","Sun and Moon face each other in opposition, the asking against the answering, and the Aquarius Rising is in trine with the Sun and in sextile with the Moon, so it is friendly to both ends of the seesaw. The manner can hold either conversation and joins whichever is louder. Two mutable lights and a fixed one: the fixed one lends the arrangement an unusual steadiness of principle, while the others range freely across ideas and countries.","Free range with good company. You can ask the question that opens a conversation, answer the one that closes it and make a stranger feel like a colleague on a long adventure. You are optimistic, original and unfailingly open to the next thing.","Freedom is the rule and the cost is hidden. You may keep every door open and walk through none, offer a lot of ideas and few promises, and be surprised that others feel unheld. The mind writes a fine argument for leaving. Growth is committing to one place and one person for a season, and writing it down."],"gemini-sagittarius-pisces":["Folding a boat from the back of a receipt at the water’s edge, you grin and get ready to push it out. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and shape-shifting, which lets you be exactly what a stranger needs. The Gemini Sun adds a quick mind with the next question. The Sagittarius Moon needs space, adventure and faith in tomorrow, and feels cheerful and philosophical until it is fenced in. You are an arrow in flight carrying a lantern in the rain: in love with the distance, and gentle about the landing.","This is a T-square by sign: the Gemini Sun and the Sagittarius Moon face each other in opposition, and the Pisces Rising squares them both, so all three lights are mutable and pull on each other. Jupiter rules the Moon and shares the Rising, which gives need and manner the same faith and the same appetite for the far shore. The Sun asks and the Moon answers, and the Rising dissolves the edges of both.","Hopeful tenderness. You can set a friend’s spirits sailing with one sentence, take a risk in a way that feels safe to watch and bring a gentle optimism to a hard week. You are a good listener who gives great directions.","With everything mutable and nothing fixed, you may leave when feeling gets heavy, call the leaving faith and let a promise drift out to sea. Others project reliability onto you and are puzzled. Growth is writing one promise down and keeping it through the dull middle."],"gemini-capricorn-aries":["By fifty you will understand that the reserve you took for coldness was a good instinct about timing, and the speed you were embarrassed by was courage that had not yet learned its season. The Aries Rising goes first. The Capricorn Moon, a square away, feels privately and manages feeling like a task, so the dash is followed by a long, serious pause. Your Gemini Sun talks its way between the two, making jokes where a plan would be better. People see a quick, funny starter. Later they see someone who always finishes.","The Capricorn Moon squares the Aries Rising, both cardinal, so the need for structure and the habit of leaping meet at a right angle and neither backs down. The Gemini Sun sits at an awkward remove from the Moon and makes a friendly sextile with the Rising, so curiosity sides with the leap and the Moon is left to supply the discipline. The Moon sits in detriment here, working against the grain, so softness has to be learned. Each light is a different kind of fast.","Ambition with a sense of humour. You can plan seriously and act boldly, and you make hard work sound like a good story. You are capable of long preparation for a quick, perfectly timed move, and others trust you to lead because you are both brave and prepared.","The Moon does the worrying silently and the Rising does the leaping loudly, so people see confidence and miss the strain. The Sun supplies a joke to cover the gap. Growth is saying “this is heavy” to someone who can help carry it, and letting the answer be slow."],"gemini-capricorn-taurus":["You are the friendliest voice at the table and the one who tells the least about yourself, and both are completely sincere. The Gemini Sun trades stories, jokes and questions all evening. The Capricorn Moon feels privately and manages feeling like a task, so it is the one in the back with the accounts. The Taurus Rising, in easy trine with it, gives you the lovely voice and the unhurried calm that make this arrangement look effortless. You are a loom with a telegraph line attached: steady work, and quick news.","Two earth lights and an air Sun. Capricorn Moon and Taurus Rising are a trine, so need and manner cooperate with ease: reserved, reliable, built to last. The Gemini Sun is the outsider, at an awkward remove from the Moon and a sign from the Rising, curious and chatty in a household that prefers to be useful. The Moon sits in detriment here, working against the grain, so gentleness has to be learned. The Sun supplies the conversation, the others supply the foundation.","Reliable wit. You can make a serious subject sound easy, you meet deadlines with a smile and you keep your promises without announcing them. You are a calm presence in a messy room, and the kind of colleague, friend or parent who makes a plan and makes people laugh while it is carried out.","Feeling is managed like a task and discussed like a topic, so what is happening in you can be described precisely and still go unfelt. The Rising makes it all look composed. Growth is letting one feeling stay unorganised for an evening, and telling one person, without a joke, that it is there."],"gemini-capricorn-gemini":["You carry it in the jaw and between the shoulder blades: a held posture, a slight bracing that most people read as composure. Your Gemini Sun and Gemini Rising are open and chatty, quick to joke and quick to ask. The Capricorn Moon feels privately and manages feeling like a task, and needs structure, competence and respect. So you look unguarded and are in fact rationing, generous with information and thrifty with everything else.","The Capricorn Moon is a quincunx to both Gemini lights, so the two sides have no common ground: no shared element, no shared mode, a house of light talk beside a house of long duty. The Moon sits in detriment, working against the grain, so tenderness has to be learned like a language. The Sun and Rising supply the chat and the Moon the discipline, and the result is a reliable talker with a very private ledger.","Measured wit. You can be funny and dependable, explain a hard thing simply and meet a deadline without losing the room. Your reserve gives your words weight: when you do say you care, it lands, because you rarely say it twice.","Feeling is treated as a project to be managed, so tenderness arrives late, scheduled and understated, and others may miss it. You can smile through a long fatigue. Growth is letting one feeling be seen while it is still unfinished, and asking for help before the list is done."],"gemini-capricorn-cancer":["An oyster builds a pearl one thin coat at a time, around an irritation, in the dark, and nobody sees anything until it is done. That is how you handle a feeling: privately, slowly, as a task, until it turns into something you can hand over. The Cancer Rising looks tender and attentive, and the Gemini Sun keeps the conversation light and quick. The Capricorn Moon is the one on duty, needing structure, competence and respect. Your warmth arrives as provision: the lift to the airport, the lasagna, the sorted taxes.","Your Capricorn Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, so what it needs it has to learn to ask for rather than assume. It sits in opposition to the Cancer Rising, the axis of home and duty seen from both ends: the front is soft, the need is a ledger, and each notices the other’s neglect. Cancer Rising is ruled by the Moon, so that sober Moon quietly steers the tender door.","Tenderness that holds weight. You show up with the practical thing, remember the date and keep the promise, and you are funny enough that people do not notice how carefully you are looking after them. In a crisis you are calm, useful and kind, and the kindness lasts after the crisis has passed.","Tenderness gets delivered as errands, and you may be hurt that nobody read the lasagna as love. You manage feelings like tasks, say you are fine and work past tiredness. Growth is saying the soft sentence aloud, once, plainly, to the person it is for, without a task attached."],"gemini-capricorn-leo":["Have I earned this yet? You ask it with the applause still in the air, and the question arrives before the pleasure does. The Leo Rising makes the entrance easy: warm, upright, quick to the right word. The Gemini Sun is the entertainer behind it, curious and light on its feet. The Capricorn Moon is the auditor in the back row, wanting structure, competence and respect, and managing its feelings as a task. The room sees a natural, and you know how many drafts there were.","Sun and Rising stand in sextile, an easy partnership of air and fire, and both sit a quincunx from the Moon: the shape is a yod by sign, two lights pointing at a third. The one pointed at, the Capricorn Moon, is in detriment and works against its grain, so it has to learn what it needs rather than assume it. The Sun rules the Leo Rising, which makes the quick mind chart ruler. The Moon’s task is slow, and the other two keep inviting it to hurry.","Reliable brilliance. You can charm the room and then do the work that justifies the charm, and the work is usually on time. People trust your promises because you quietly count them. Your warmth arrives as provision, and your standards make others a little braver.","Pleasure arrives with a bill attached. You may discount a compliment, work through the interval or save the enjoyment for when the job is finished, and then find it is never finished. Feelings are handled like tasks and filed. Growth is letting one good evening be paid for in advance, and saying thank you without the audit."],"gemini-capricorn-virgo":["Given time you will see that the long ascent was never the point and the needle and thread were. For now the Virgo Rising is modest, tidy and quietly capable, and the Gemini Sun is the light conversationalist who makes it look easy. The Capricorn Moon is where the weight sits. It feels privately, manages feeling like a task and needs structure, competence and respect. People think you are cool and capable. You are, and you also carry more than anyone knows.","The Capricorn Moon and the Virgo Rising are both earth and in trine, so need and manner agree about almost everything: quality, thrift, doing the thing properly. The Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, so it learns by effort what other Moons assume. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from the Moon and a square from the Rising, so the mind keeps proposing something lighter to a house that has already decided.","Dependable quickness. You can learn the system, do the work and explain it to the next person without condescension. Your word is kept, your corrections are kind and your humour is dry and well timed. Over the years you become the person others hand the important thing to.","Duty can swallow joy. You may do the sensible thing so reliably that nobody asks what you want, and call tiredness a standard. Feeling arrives as provision and as a clipped reply. Growth is a rule broken on purpose now and then, a day with no thread in it, and a request made in plain words."],"gemini-capricorn-libra":["You make charm look effortless, and it is the most carefully built thing you own. The Libra Rising does the visible work: gracious, symmetrical, exactly the right distance. The Gemini Sun adds a quick mind that keeps the conversation bright. The Capricorn Moon is the foundation nobody sees. It feels privately, manages feeling as a task and needs structure, competence and respect, so every graceful evening has hours of preparation under it. Others get ease. You get the schedule.","The Capricorn Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, and it stands in square to the Libra Rising, both cardinal, earth against air: the need wants structure and the manner wants everyone comfortable. The Gemini Sun is a trine from the Rising and a quincunx from the Moon, so it moves easily on the surface and has to translate for the Moon. The Moon’s care arrives as provision, and the manner makes it look like charm.","Grace with reliability. You can charm a room and then deliver, keep the promise made at the party and do so quietly. Others lean on your steadiness without noticing the work. You build things that outlast the evening, and make that look pleasant.","The front is so smooth that nobody checks what it costs. You may be thanked for the evening and never for the weeks of work, and let it pass. Feeling is managed as a task and delivered as a favour. Growth is saying “this was hard” to one person, and receiving the thank you for the real thing."],"gemini-capricorn-scorpio":["Your jaw sets and your shoulders square before you have found the feeling to attach to it, and you stand like someone waiting for a train that will be exactly on time. The Scorpio Rising makes the stillness look deliberate: guarded, magnetic, slightly impossible to read. The Gemini Sun keeps the talk dry and quick. The Capricorn Moon feels privately, manages feeling as a task and needs structure, competence and respect. The tower keeps the hours, and what it has burnt through is quietly swept up.","The Capricorn Moon and the Scorpio Rising are in sextile, earth and water, so need and manner cooperate and look alike: serious, patient with time and slow to reveal. This makes the Gemini Sun the apex of a yod by sign, a quincunx from both, with neither element nor mode in common with either. The mind is the one light that must adjust. The Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, and learns by effort what other Moons assume.","Endurance with edge. You can do long, hard, quiet work and keep your own counsel, and you notice when something is off and fix it before it is noticed. You are formidable under pressure, and dry enough to make pressure funny.","Feeling is filed rather than felt. You may work through grief, tell a friend you are fine and call it strength, or keep a score that nobody else knows exists. The mind describes the weather and avoids the climate. Growth is leaving one hour a week unscheduled, and letting whatever rises in it go unmanaged."],"gemini-capricorn-sagittarius":["A compass needle spends its whole life trembling, and every tremor is in the service of one steady direction. That is your arrangement. The Sagittarius Rising arrives bright, restless and laughing, with news, and people feel invited to widen their lives. Your Gemini Sun keeps the talk quick and the notes in the margin. The Capricorn Moon is the part that steadies: it feels privately, manages feeling like a task and needs structure, competence and respect. The openness is real. So is the foundation nobody sees.","The Capricorn Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, and sits a semi-sextile from the Sagittarius Rising, so manner and need are neighbours who barely see each other: one is wide open and one is held in. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from the Moon and an opposition to the Rising, so the mind has to translate between a laugh and a ledger. The Moon is the slow learner, and the one that keeps the others honest.","Optimism with a spine. You can say yes to a big idea and then do the plain work that makes it happen, and you keep a promise made at a party. You mix play and discipline, and you teach by example.","The needle trembles, and you may call it fine. You may treat tiredness as a standard, give more than you have and be hurt that nobody asked about the cost. Feeling is filed and scheduled. Growth is saying out loud what you need before the journey, and letting a day be wasted on purpose."],"gemini-capricorn-capricorn":["Is it all right to be warm yet? You ask it of yourself in a winter kitchen, and the answer usually arrives as a list. Moon and Rising share Capricorn, so what you need and how you arrive are the same: composed, dry, responsible and a little older than the calendar. The Gemini Sun is the visitor from a younger country, curious, funny and always asking what else is out there. You were handed gravity early. The mind has been quietly keeping the lightness.","Moon and Rising share Capricorn, a doubled sign, and the Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, so it learns by effort what other Moons assume: how to say what it needs. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from both, sharing neither element nor mode, which makes the mind a permanent guest in a sober house. Two lights keep the hours and one keeps asking whether anyone would like to go outside.","Dependable wit. You can carry a long project with a dry joke on top, advise with authority and a light touch and stay steady when others are not. People rely on you and are glad of the humour. Over time you become the person others hand the important thing to.","Duty can become a habit of not asking. You may do the sensible thing so consistently that nobody knows what you want, and file feeling under provision. Frost keeps well. Growth is letting one afternoon be useless, and saying the warm sentence before it has been earned."],"gemini-capricorn-aquarius":["Eventually you will see that what you called duty was the most original structure you ever built. For now the Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance, a person slightly ahead of the present moment. The Gemini Sun keeps the talk quick and the ideas many. The Capricorn Moon feels privately, manages feeling like a task and needs structure, competence and respect. You are the one who draws the constellation as a network and then walks the ridge to check the distances.","Saturn rules the Capricorn Moon and shares the Aquarius Rising, so the Moon and the Rising borrow a planet: both respect structure, and both prefer to reach the future by sensible routes. The two sit a semi-sextile apart and barely see each other: the cool friendliness in front, the careful duty behind. The Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, and learns by effort what other Moons assume. The Gemini Sun is a trine from the Rising and a quincunx from the Moon.","Practical vision. You can imagine a better arrangement and then pace out the ground, mind the budget and keep the promise. Your ideas arrive with a schedule, your friendships with a long memory and your humour with a straight face.","Provision stands in for closeness. You may build a good thing for someone and not say you care, treat tiredness as a standard and keep your own needs on a waiting list. The cool face assists. Growth is saying one plain, warm sentence to the person the structure is for."],"gemini-capricorn-pisces":["You are a very practical person with a very impractical face, and both are correct. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and faraway, and strangers decide you are a dreamer before you have spoken. The Gemini Sun is the quick, curious mind that keeps the options open. The Capricorn Moon feels privately, manages feeling like a task and needs structure, competence and respect. It is the mountain path to the face’s ocean floor: the same ground, seen from above and from below.","The Capricorn Moon is in sextile with the Pisces Rising, earth and water, so feeling and manner help each other: the water has a shore and the shore has a view. The Moon is in detriment, working against its grain, and learns by effort what other Moons assume. The Gemini Sun is a quincunx from the Moon and a square from the Rising, sharing no element or mode with the first and clashing with the second, so the mind is the restless guest in a house with good bones.","Structure with soul. You can make a dream into a plan and a plan into a kindness, hold a boundary gently, and keep a promise with a mist of warmth around it. You are patient with ideas and exact with deadlines.","Duty and diffusion can alternate. You may work hard to avoid a feeling, or let the feeling soak the work until nothing is finished. Tenderness arrives as provision, and the face blurs the message. Growth is saying one soft thing out loud, in plain words, to the person it concerns."],"gemini-aquarius-aries":["After the meeting has ended, you are still at the whiteboard, drawing lines between people who have never met and saying “those two should talk”. The Aries Rising makes the first call, usually before the plan is finished. The Aquarius Moon, friendly and cool, needs freedom, friendship and room to be strange. Your Gemini Sun, in trine with it, is the messenger who carries the idea from one corner of the network to another. People find you quick, generous and a little hard to pin to one group.","Two air lights and a fire Rising make an arc of ease: Gemini Sun and Aquarius Moon are a trine, and the Aries Rising makes a friendly sextile with each, so the three lights cooperate and almost nothing is in conflict. Ideas flow, the manner pushes them into action, and the Moon asks only that nobody try to own the result. The ease is the risk: with no friction, the chart can stay brilliant and unfinished, a very good network that never builds a house.","Inventive connection. You introduce people, ideas and fields that should have met earlier, you act on a good thought before it cools, and you leave others feeling that the future is slightly more possible. You are generous with credit and unbothered by convention.","Everything flows, so nothing is forced to land. The Moon prefers detachment, the Rising prefers motion and the Sun enjoys the discussion, so plans stay as constellations. Growth is picking one line on the whiteboard and doing the dull work of making it a bridge."],"gemini-aquarius-taurus":["People take the calm, friendly manner for conventionality, and are startled by the first idea you share. The Taurus Rising gives you a lovely voice, an unhurried air and the look of someone who owns a good coat and a regular parking space. The Aquarius Moon, a square away, needs friends, freedom and room to be strange. Your Gemini Sun, in easy trine with the Moon, is the one who has read about the satellite pass and will tell you, at length, when to look up. The surface is traditional. The household is not.","Two air lights and an earth Rising. Gemini Sun and Aquarius Moon are a trine, so curiosity and the need for freedom run together as easily as two friends on a long walk. The Taurus Rising squares the Moon, both fixed, so the settled, sensual manner argues stubbornly with the need to be odd and unattached. It stands a sign from the Sun. The result is an experimental mind in a conservative coat, and a good deal of friction about when to take it off.","Friendly originality. You make the unusual sound welcoming, you introduce new ideas without alarming anyone and you have the patience to see them through. People trust you with change because you look as if you would never rush it, and you hold the door for those who do.","The Rising resists change and the Moon demands it, so you can argue for freedom in the evening and keep the same routine in the morning. The Sun enjoys the discussion. Growth is changing one fixed habit this week and telling a friend, who will not let you quietly revert."],"gemini-aquarius-gemini":["Three in the morning is your hour: the house is quiet, a friend in another time zone is awake, and ideas move at the speed of typing. The Gemini Sun and Gemini Rising make you easy company by day, curious and quick with strangers. The Aquarius Moon needs freedom, friendship and room to be strange, and is happiest a small distance from the crowd, close to people rather than inside them. You are friendly and a little unattached, a writer of letters in a time of messages.","Everything here is air, and the Aquarius Moon makes a trine to both Gemini lights: ideas, distance and conversation are native to all three, so the need and the manner agree. That ease is real, and so is its price, because nothing pushes you from the head into the body. The Moon is fixed while the Sun and Rising are mutable, so friendships last far longer than the topics that began them.","Open-minded loyalty. You can befriend almost anyone, hold a position without a grudge and see where a group is heading before it does. You are a good connector of people, ideas and favours, and you make others feel interesting.","Distance can feel like freedom when it is also avoidance, and affection that arrives as an interesting link may not read as warmth. You can be present everywhere and nowhere in particular. Growth is staying in one conversation until it turns personal, and saying “I missed you” without a footnote."],"gemini-aquarius-cancer":["When closeness gets too close, you become friendlier and more distant at once: a longer message, a warmer tone, an hour’s walk before you reply. The Cancer Rising invites people in, remembers their troubles and puts the kettle on. The Gemini Sun keeps the conversation quick and the world interesting. The Aquarius Moon needs friendship, freedom and room to be strange. You post paper boats, small, kind, odd messages sent down the river to people you love, and you are glad when they arrive.","The Aquarius Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, two airs, so mind and need agree easily and the ideas feel like feelings. The Cancer Rising is the difficult light: it stands a quincunx from the Moon, sharing neither element nor mode, so the front invites closeness that the Moon wants only in measured doses. Cancer Rising is ruled by the Moon, which makes the freedom-loving Moon the chart ruler, and the door you hold open is meant to swing both ways.","Warmth without possession. You befriend all sorts of people, let them be odd and remember them across years and distances. You offer care and room in the same gesture, which is rare and reassuring, and you are good at the long, kind, funny letter.","Closeness is welcomed with the door open and one foot out. You may seem present and be elsewhere, or answer a need with an idea, and people who wanted warmth may feel they were handed a pamphlet. Growth is saying “I need two days” instead of fading, and letting one person see you being ordinary and needy."],"gemini-aquarius-leo":["Your inner house has three residents who want different things. The Gemini Sun is at the kitchen table with the newspapers, wanting to know what everyone thinks. The Leo Rising is on the stairs in a good jacket, wanting to be seen coming down. The Aquarius Moon is on the roof with a telescope, wanting nobody to ask why. Guests meet the one on the stairs and enjoy the one at the table, and sometimes look up and wonder who is on the roof.","Moon and Rising sit in opposition, Aquarius across from Leo: a need for friendship at a distance faces a manner of warmth up close, like two doors in one hall. The Sun in Gemini is a trine from the Moon and a sextile from the Rising, so it speaks both languages and can carry a message either way. It also rules the Rising, so the quick mind is chart ruler, and a good deal of your life is spent translating.","Warm detachment, which is rarer than it sounds. You can hold a view without needing agreement, be glad of other people’s differences and give a crowd your full attention without clinging to it. Your humour includes the odd, the old and the very young, and your friendships last for decades at a comfortable distance.","The gaze people take for warmth may be partly a telescope. You can perform closeness and keep a safe distance, give attention to everyone and be known by few, and call it independence. Others feel handled. Growth is letting one friend into the ordinary, unlit hour, and staying a little past comfortable."],"gemini-aquarius-virgo":["In the middle of a crisis you are the one who quietly opens a window, not to escape but to let some air through. The Virgo Rising is observant and modest, already mending what is broken. The Gemini Sun adds a quick, friendly mind that keeps the talk moving. The Aquarius Moon needs friendship, freedom and room to be strange, and it watches the fuss from slightly further back than anyone notices. You are calm, helpful and a little elsewhere, which makes you both reassuring and hard to pin down.","The Aquarius Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, two airs, so thinking and feeling understand each other and the ideas feel like feelings. The Virgo Rising is the awkward light: a square from the Sun, though Mercury rules them both, and a quincunx from the Moon, with neither element nor mode in common. The front is practical and close, the need is detached and wide, and a fair amount of your life is spent being useful from a respectful distance.","Cool, constructive kindness. You can help without making a scene, work in a team without being swallowed by it and let people be strange. You fix things, spot the pattern and have a gift for solutions that are original and also actually work.","Helpfulness at a distance can feel like absence. You may solve a person’s problem and leave without sitting in it, or file your own feeling under interesting. Closeness is welcome in small doses. Growth is staying through the awkward part of one conversation, and saying “I care about this” in a sentence with no analysis in it."],"gemini-aquarius-libra":["Everyone assumes you are the easy, sociable one with no edges. What they have not seen is how much of you is a window left open on purpose. The Libra Rising is gracious and symmetrical and makes everyone feel considered. Your Gemini Sun offers a quick, friendly mind at the party. The Aquarius Moon needs freedom, friendship and room to be strange, and it feels through ideas and distance. You are less social than you look and more loyal than you say.","Sun, Moon and Rising are all air, so this is a grand trine by sign: a closed circuit of ease, each light in trine with the other two, and every modality different. Everything flows, which is why you can be warm in company and a hermit in the evening with no strain. The shape has no friction and no outside view. Nobody in the circuit asks what you would do if you were not charming, curious or free.","Easy originality. You can befriend almost anyone, bring a strange idea into a drawing room and make it welcome, and defend someone else’s difference without making them feel defended. Your friendships are wide, your humour is kind and your independence is generous.","With everything flowing, you can drift. You may agree to a lot, keep your real thoughts in the window and be a stranger to people who thought they were close. The circuit is pleasant and has no ground. Growth is making one plain request each week, and letting somebody fail to guess a need rather than hiding it."],"gemini-aquarius-scorpio":["At three in the morning you notice the message nobody else saw and quietly answer it. The Scorpio Rising looks guarded and steady, with a gaze people feel before they understand it. The Gemini Sun is the quick, curious mind that keeps a signal tower of friends. The Aquarius Moon needs freedom, friendship and room to be strange, and feels through ideas and distance. You appear intense and are in fact fond of everyone at a distance, which is how you manage to be so reliable.","Moon and Rising are both fixed and in square, air against water: a need for distance and freedom faces a manner of depth and gravity, and neither will give way. The Gemini Sun is a trine from the Moon, so thought and need are good friends, and a quincunx from the Rising, so the mind and the stare do not share a language. The mind and the Moon talk easily from the tower, while the Rising stands guard at the door.","Loyal detachment. You can watch a situation without panic, send the right message at the right hour and keep a friendship alive across years of silence. You read people accurately, let them be strange and have a gift for understanding what goes unsaid.","Fixed against fixed, you can dig in. You may call a retreat independence, keep your feelings in the tower and your friends at the foot of it, or watch a hurt grow and discuss it as an idea. Growth is climbing down for one evening, and letting someone see you tired rather than interesting."],"gemini-aquarius-sagittarius":["In a good mood you invite everyone, and when tired you vanish politely, with a wave and a promise to write. The Sagittarius Rising arrives bright, restless and laughing, with news, and people feel invited to widen their lives. The Gemini Sun is the quick mind at the signal tower, forever sending and receiving. The Aquarius Moon needs freedom, friendship and room to be strange, and feels through ideas and distance. You are the host who keeps a window open and a bag by the door.","The Aquarius Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun and in sextile with the Sagittarius Rising, so the need is friendly to mind and manner alike, and the three agree on freedom, ideas and company. The Sun and the Rising are in opposition, the one question the arrangement keeps asking: detail or horizon. The Moon says both, as long as nobody takes the door off.","Friendly range. You can gather people who would never meet, let each be odd in their own way and keep a friendship going across continents. You are good at ideas and kind about people, and hard to bore or to corner.","Freedom can become a way of never being pinned. You may be everywhere and known by few, answer a need with an article, or leave a gathering just before it turns intimate. Others feel welcomed and not held. Growth is staying through the hour when it becomes personal, and offering something small and true."],"gemini-aquarius-capricorn":["Imagine a house with three residents and one front door. The Gemini Sun is in the library at dusk with a pencil, linking one book to another. The Capricorn Rising is in the front office, composed and dry, keeping the hours and holding the keys. The Aquarius Moon is at the window with a telescope, drawing the constellations as a network and wanting to be left alone with it. Visitors are met in the office, and a few are offered a chair in the library.","Saturn rules the Capricorn Rising and shares the Aquarius Moon, so manner and need borrow a planet: both value structure, and both prefer to arrive at the future by sensible routes. The two sit a semi-sextile apart, neighbours with a wall between them, so the front and the need hardly meet. The Gemini Sun is a trine from the Moon, so thought and need are friends, and a quincunx from the Rising, so the mind keeps leaving the front office by the window.","Steady reform. You can see how a system could be better, then build it in a way that nobody notices until it works. You are fair, original and dry, a friend to the odd and a reliable colleague, and your ideas arrive with a timetable.","Distance can pass for responsibility. You may handle everyone’s needs from the front office and keep your own in the tower, let a friendship cool to a pleasant correspondence and call it freedom. Growth is bringing one person up the stairs to the telescope, and letting them see what you are drawing."],"gemini-aquarius-aquarius":["Coat still on, at the edge of the room, you listen to the conversation like someone enjoying an interesting radio. Moon and Rising share Aquarius, so what you need and how you arrive are one cool, unusual, friendly thing that wants freedom, friendship and room to be strange. The Gemini Sun gives it a voice: curious, quick, a little ahead of the news. People like you at once. They find the door has no handle on the outside, and that you open it when you decide to.","Moon and Rising share Aquarius, a doubled sign, so what you need and how you arrive are the same: friendly, free and slightly ahead of the moment. The Gemini Sun is in trine with both, air with air, so mind, need and manner share an easy language. All three are air, and two are fixed. There is little friction and no outside view. Saturn and Uranus rule the two heavy lights: the principles are stable and the opinions are original.","Cool warmth. You can befriend a stranger, hold a view without needing it admired, defend someone’s right to be odd and remain steady in a crisis. You are loyal at a distance, a quiet constant. Your ideas are fresh, and they are kind.","The easy circuit has no outside view. You may keep everyone at a friendly range and be known by almost nobody, treat a need as a flaw in the plan, or leave by the door that only opens from your side. Growth is leaving the door open for one person, and letting them see you want them to come in."],"gemini-aquarius-pisces":["Strangers assume you are the dreamy, agreeable sort who will go along with anything. In fact your opinions are firm, and you keep them far offshore. The Pisces Rising is gentle, receptive and faraway, and people project onto it all sorts of things. The Gemini Sun offers a quick, curious mind. The Aquarius Moon needs freedom, friendship and room to be strange, and feels through ideas and distance. You are a visitor in every crowd, friendly to the weather and a little apart from it.","The Aquarius Moon is in trine with the Gemini Sun, air with air, so thought and need are friends and the ideas feel like feelings. The Pisces Rising is a square from the Sun, both mutable, and a semi-sextile from the Moon: the manner is soft, shared and absorbent, and the Moon is cool, individual and slightly aloof. They are neighbours who borrow each other’s weather and rarely speak about it.","Gentle independence. You can be warm with everyone and owned by nobody, let people be strange and take their strangeness seriously, and hold a view with courtesy. You listen well, change slowly and make a refreshing sort of friend.","The soft face invites closeness and the cool Moon takes a step back, so people feel invited and then left. You may leave a gathering at the point of greatest warmth, or answer a feeling with an idea. Growth is staying one minute past the point where you would normally slip out, and saying what the minute is like."],"gemini-pisces-aries":["An hour of talk can leave nothing said, and a minute of silence can leave everything said. The Gemini Sun is a mind that thinks by speaking, and the Aries Rising speaks first and fastest. The Pisces Moon, a neighbour to the Rising and square to the Sun, feels what belongs to other people as well as what belongs to you, and needs music, water and solitude to sort it. People get the chatter. You get the hymn heard through the wall.","Gemini Sun and Pisces Moon square each other, both mutable, so mind and feeling keep crossing: the Sun wants to name things, the Moon wants to dissolve them. The Aries Rising sits one sign from the Moon, which means the quick, direct front door is bolted onto a very porous room. Three different elements and no shared ground make for variety and a certain loneliness. The Rising acts, the Moon absorbs, and the Sun tries to keep up with the commentary.","Imaginative quickness. You catch a mood and make it into a story, a song or a joke before others have noticed it, and you can enter a stranger’s feeling without losing your own footing for long. Your gifts show most in words, music and the small act of timing a kindness perfectly.","Absorbing everyone’s weather and then outrunning your own, you may leave a room tired in a way that nothing explains. Talk is used to dilute the feeling. Growth is a regular silence with water or music in it, and one friend to whom you say the true thing without the joke."],"gemini-pisces-taurus":["You carry it in the hands and the breath: hands that fold, shape and fidget as if working something that cannot be said, and a breath held a little high in the chest. The Pisces Moon feels everything, including what belongs to others, and needs solitude, music and water to find its edges. The Taurus Rising, a friendly sextile away, gives the whole matter a calm, solid, lovely-voiced front, so nobody guesses. Your Gemini Sun squares the Moon and talks, folding feelings into paper boats and setting them on the current.","Gemini Sun and Pisces Moon square each other, both mutable, so thought and feeling keep crossing: the Sun wants to name, the Moon wants to dissolve. The Taurus Rising is a friendly sextile to the Moon and a neighbour to the Sun, so the manner supports the water, giving it a shore, a voice and a routine. The effect is a porous interior inside a very well-behaved exterior. Venus smooths the surface, Neptune loosens what lies under it, and Mercury attempts to keep notes.","Gentle fluency. You can talk someone through a sorrow without making them feel managed, find the right word at the right time and make something beautiful out of a passing mood. People feel safe near the calm and understood by the words, and often come back for both.","Absorbing the room’s feelings behind a calm face, you may be exhausted without a visible cause. The Sun explains it as tiredness, a busy week, anything but weather. Growth is asking, quietly and often, which of these feelings are yours, and giving the water an hour alone each day."],"gemini-pisces-gemini":["Imagine a page of handwriting that runs to the margin and keeps going until the ink becomes a stream. The Gemini Sun and Gemini Rising are the neat, quick lines, funny and well organised in company. The Pisces Moon is the water beneath them: it feels everything, including what belongs to others, and needs solitude, music and permission to drift. You can be exact in the morning and dissolved by evening, and neither is a pose.","The Pisces Moon squares both Gemini lights, and all three signs are mutable, so the friction is restless: three adjustable lights and no fixed point to lean on. The mind sorts and the Moon dissolves, and what the Sun has just put in order the evening washes loose again. Each is honest, and neither is in charge. You are at your best when the sorting is allowed to be a way of listening.","Intuitive language. You can say what a room is feeling before it knows, write a line that lands as music and listen in a way that lets people stop explaining. Your imagination is generous, and your kindness is exact.","Other people’s moods enter you through conversation, and you may not know whose they are. The remedy you reach for is more talking, which only widens the water. Growth is a daily hour with no input and no output, and a plain sentence of your own at the end of it."],"gemini-pisces-cancer":["Whose feeling is this? You ask it in corridors, in shops and in the middle of conversations that were going perfectly well, and half the time the answer is: not yours. The Cancer Rising takes people in, the Pisces Moon absorbs what they bring, and the Gemini Sun tries to describe it all in a sentence or two. Music, water and an hour alone put you back together. To the world you seem sweet, quick and mildly vague. To the few who stay, you are the one who always knew.","Two of your lights are water and in an easy trine, the Cancer Rising and the Pisces Moon, so the front and the need both let feeling through without a gate. Cancer Rising is ruled by the Moon, so the Pisces Moon sets the tide at the door. The Gemini Sun sits in a square to the Moon, mutable against mutable, air against water, and its habit is to explain what the Moon only wants to dissolve. That friction is also your craft: finding words for what has none.","Attunement with language. You feel what someone is carrying and find the words for it, gently, before they have asked. You are a soothing voice at a bedside, a good ear on a long call and someone who can turn a mood into a song, a sentence or a meal.","Other people’s moods enter by the open front, and the mind explains them as yours. You may sleep, scroll or wander off to dissolve what you cannot sort, and boundaries are learned slowly. Growth is a small ritual after company, ten quiet minutes by water or music, and the habit of asking whether a feeling is yours or borrowed before acting on it."],"gemini-pisces-leo":["An older relative would say that what you took for stage fright was other people’s weather, and that you were never the only one trembling in the wings. For now the Leo Rising walks on lit and warm, your Gemini Sun supplies a quick, funny line, and the Pisces Moon feels the whole house breathe. Music, water and an hour alone set you right. The audience sees a confident entrance. The few close to you know it is also a gift.","Sun and Moon are in square, mutable against mutable, air against water: the mind wants to describe and the heart wants to dissolve. The Leo Rising is a sextile from the Sun and a quincunx from the Moon, so the stage is easy for the talker and awkward for the sponge. The Sun rules your Rising, which makes it chart ruler, and a good part of the work is finding sentences that carry what the Moon takes in without drowning it.","Performance with attunement. You can read a room’s mood and give it back a little lighter: the right joke, the right song, the right pause. You are a natural host, a healer of dull evenings and a storyteller who knows what each listener most needs to hear.","Other people’s moods come in through the lit front door, and you may play them back as your own. You can pour yourself out on the stage and collapse afterwards, or slip away into music, sleep or a small fantasy. Boundaries are learned slowly. Growth is a fixed hour of quiet after any big evening, and a plain question, whose is this, before acting on a feeling."],"gemini-pisces-virgo":["You keep a very tidy desk and a completely open heart, and the second is the reason for the first. The Virgo Rising is modest, observant and careful, the person who sorts the pens and the envelopes. The Gemini Sun offers a quick, funny mind that explains everything gently. The Pisces Moon feels what belongs to everyone else, and needs solitude, music and water. Order is how you stay afloat. People meet the tidy surface and rely on it, and do not know how much it is holding back.","All three lights are mutable and each is a different element, so this is a T-square by sign: the Pisces Moon opposes the Virgo Rising, and the Gemini Sun squares them both. Moon and Rising sit on one axis, feeling against order, dissolving against sorting, and the Sun swings between them with a sentence for each side. Mercury rules Sun and Rising, so the arguments are conducted in good prose. The pressure builds slowly, and the workbench sometimes floods.","Careful compassion. You can sense what is wrong and know what to do about it, sit with a person and still find the practical next step. You are a natural nurse, editor or fixer of quiet crises. Your help is gentle, exact and unshowy.","The dam and the flood take turns. You may keep everything in order until the order is the problem, then dissolve into music, sleep or a fog of worry. Other people’s moods become another list of things to fix. Growth is a daily open hour with no tasks in it, and the habit of asking whose feeling you have picked up."],"gemini-pisces-libra":["A pressure sits behind your breastbone when the room is out of tune, and your breath goes shallow while your smile stays perfectly even. The Libra Rising is gracious, symmetrical and quick to ease a moment. Your Gemini Sun keeps the talk light and well informed. The Pisces Moon feels everything, including what belongs to other people, and needs solitude, music and water to put itself right. Guests see poise. The few close to you know it is a ribbon laid over a current.","Sun and Moon are in square, mutable against mutable, air against water: the mind wants to name and the heart wants to dissolve. The Libra Rising is a trine from the Sun and a quincunx from the Moon, so the surface is in easy conversation with the mind and shares nothing with the heart. That gap is hidden by good manners, which is partly what the manners are for.","Tact with a sixth sense. You sense what a person needs and offer it so gracefully they do not feel handled. You are a gifted listener, a soothing guest and someone who can tell a hard truth in a way that arrives as a kindness.","Other people’s moods flow in and are then managed by smiling. You may agree with several people in one evening, absorb all their weather and go home empty. Boundaries are learned slowly. Growth is an hour of water or music after company, and a plain sentence of no that does not need to be pretty."],"gemini-pisces-scorpio":["A hymn heard through a wall loses its words and keeps its weather. That is how people receive you. The Scorpio Rising is the wall, guarded and charged, and the Gemini Sun brings a quick, kind voice at the door. The Pisces Moon is the hymn: it feels everything, including what belongs to others, and needs solitude, music and water. Two lights are water and in trine, so the feeling is deep and shared between them. One is air and square to the Moon, so the mind keeps trying to write down the tune.","The Pisces Moon and the Scorpio Rising are in trine, water with water, so the Moon and the Rising understand each other without a word and the interior is a large, quiet, shared sea. The Gemini Sun is a square from the Moon, mutable against mutable, the habit of naming against the wish to dissolve, and a quincunx from the Rising, which shares nothing with it. The mind is the one light that must translate, and it works hard.","Attunement with discretion. You sense what a person is carrying and respond without making them say it, hold other people’s secrets and moods with a steady hand, and find words for a feeling that has none. You are a gifted listener, a quiet healer and a good translator of silence.","The wall protects and also muffles. Other people’s feelings pass through you unmarked, and you may take them on as your own and say nothing. Boundaries are learned slowly. Growth is leaving the door ajar for one person, and saying aloud whose feeling it is."],"gemini-pisces-sagittarius":["Is this a leap of faith, or am I just leaving? You ask it at the edge of every cliff and every difficult conversation. The Sagittarius Rising arrives bright, restless and laughing, with news, and people feel invited to widen their lives. Your Gemini Sun keeps asking questions and finding words. The Pisces Moon feels everything, including what belongs to others, and needs solitude, music and water. Salt on the skin, a map with no labels: you believe in tomorrow and can feel every yesterday at once.","This is a T-square by sign: the Gemini Sun and the Sagittarius Rising face each other in opposition, and the Pisces Moon squares them both, so all three lights are mutable and pull on one another. Jupiter rules the Moon and the Rising alike, which gives the feeling and the manner the same faith and the same appetite. The Sun asks and the Rising answers, and the Moon feels the cost of both.","Faith that includes feeling. You can bring hope to a sad table without denying the sadness, sense what a stranger needs and make a journey feel like a blessing. You are a good listener who tells good stories.","Faith can slide into avoidance. You may leap away from a feeling, overpromise to be kind and take in other people’s weather as if it were yours. Boundaries are learned slowly. Growth is a quiet hour after every crowd, and a plain no that does not need a story."],"gemini-pisces-capricorn":["An old friend would tell you that a handshake that means it is also a kind of tenderness, and that you were never as stern as you looked, only careful about where the water was allowed in. For now the Capricorn Rising is composed, serious and dry, a little older than the calendar. The Gemini Sun is the quick mind and the clean sentence. The Pisces Moon feels everything, including what belongs to others, and needs solitude, music and water. The office is brackish: salt and fresh water in one room.","The Pisces Moon is a sextile from the Capricorn Rising, water and earth working together, so need and manner help each other: the sea has a harbour wall and the wall has a view. The Gemini Sun is a square from the Moon, mutable against mutable, the habit of naming against the wish to dissolve, and a quincunx from the Rising, so the mind is the one light with nothing in common with either. It acts as the interpreter at the estuary.","Compassion with structure. You can feel what a person needs and turn it into a plan, sit with grief and still remember the paperwork. You hold boundaries kindly, speak plainly and keep a promise that means it.","The wall can be so good that nobody guesses what is behind it. You may absorb other people’s moods and file them as responsibilities, sleep or work to dissolve what you cannot say, and be dry about your own tiredness. Boundaries are learned slowly. Growth is a regular hour with water or music and nothing to produce."],"gemini-pisces-aquarius":["You seem to be ahead of everyone, and you feel everyone’s weather. Both are true, and neither is a performance. The Aquarius Rising is cool, unusual and friendly from a distance, which is a good altitude for a person who absorbs moods. The Gemini Sun adds a quick, clear voice that describes what it sees. The Pisces Moon feels everything, including what belongs to others, and needs solitude, music and water. The pass is brief, and the rain is long.","The Pisces Moon sits a semi-sextile from the Aquarius Rising, neighbours with one thin wall between them: the manner is cool and wide, and the need is wet and intimate. The two cannot see each other well. The Gemini Sun is in trine with the Rising, so mind and manner converse easily, and a square from the Moon, mutable against mutable: the habit of naming against the wish to dissolve. The mind is the interpreter, and the Moon rarely leaves it a clear message.","Distant compassion. You can feel what a friend far away is going through and say the right thing by message, hold a mood without being drowned by it and bring an unusual gentleness to a hard conversation. You are a good listener, a good translator and a surprising source of comfort.","Distance can be both a protection and a place to disappear. You may take on a stranger’s mood, explain it as an idea and go quiet for days. Boundaries are learned slowly. Growth is an hour of music or water after every crowded week, and saying, plainly, that you are not available."],"gemini-pisces-pisces":["Your edges soften: your shoulders drop, your eyes go to a middle distance and your hands loosen, as if the room had become a little warmer than it is. Moon and Rising share Pisces, so what you need and how you arrive are one gentle, receptive, shape-shifting thing that feels everything, including what belongs to others. The Gemini Sun brings a quick, curious voice that keeps trying to describe it. People project onto you, and you let them for a while.","Moon and Rising share Pisces, a doubled sign, and the Gemini Sun squares both, air against water, with all three mutable. The two watery lights are fluent in feeling and absorb everything nearby, and the one airy light keeps trying to name what has no name. Moon and Rising agree and the Sun is the interpreter in a house with no walls. Jupiter and Neptune rule the heavy lights, so the faith is wide and the boundaries are thin.","Wide empathy with words. You can feel what a crowd needs and say it so that people feel accompanied, make a lonely table less lonely and write a sentence that stays. You are gentle, funny, imaginative and a very welcome presence at a bedside.","Without walls, the weather comes in. You may become what the room needs, forget what you needed, and take a half remembered dream as if it were instructions. The mind keeps talking so that the dissolving feels like a plan. Growth is a small ritual of closing, like a hand on a table, to say where you end."]});
